helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	is	Trigonometric function that returns the arctangent of a numeric expression. The return value is in the range -Pi/2 to +Pi/2.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	is	The arctangent is the inverse of the tangent function. The Atn Function returns the angle "Alpha", expressed in radians, using the tangent of this angle. The function can also return the angle "Alpha" by comparing the ratio of the length of the side that is opposite of the angle to the length of the side that is adjacent to the angle in a right-angled triangle.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	is	Atn(side opposite the angle/side adjacent to angle)= Alpha				20181231 09:50:43
