helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145160	150			0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CURRENCYSYMBOL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can enter a character or a string for the currency symbol.\</ahelp\>In a currency field, you can pre-define the currency symbol by entering the character or string in the \<emph\>Currency symbol\</emph\> property.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144444				0	is	Gildi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152417	155			0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_HIDDEN_VALUE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can enter the data that is inherited by the hidden control.\</ahelp\>In a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"hidden control\"\>hidden control\</link\>, under \<emph\>Value\</emph\>, you can enter the data which is inherited by the hidden control. This data will be transferred when sending the form.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157315				0	is	Lykilorðastafir				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155323	157			0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ECHO_CHAR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If the text box is used as a password input, enter the ASCII-code of the display character. This character is displayed instead of the characters typed by the user for the password.\</ahelp\>If the user enters a password, you can determine the characters that will be displayed instead of the characters typed by the user. Under \<emph\>Password character\</emph\>, enter the ASCII code of the desired character. You can use the values from 0 to 255.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152493				0	is	The characters and their ASCII codes can be seen in the \<emph\>Special Characters\</emph\> dialog (Insert - Special Character).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157884				0	is	Orðrétt snið				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3157557	160			0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_LITERALMASK\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Defines the literal mask. The literal mask contains the initial values and is always visible after downloading a form.\</ahelp\>With masked fields you can specify a literal mask. A literal mask contains the initial values of a form, and is always visible after downloading a form. Using a character code for the Edit mask, you can determine the entries that the user can type into the masked field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148513				0	is	The length of the literal mask should always correspond to the length of the edit mask. If this is not the case, the edit mask is either cut off or filled with blanks up to the length of the edit mask.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146762				0	is	Letur				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151037	6			0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_FONT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the font for the text that is in the control field.\</ahelp\>For control fields which have visible text or titles, select the display font that you want to use. To open the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Font\"\>\<emph\>Font\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button. The selected font is used in control fields names and to display data in table control fields.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156734				0	is	Hæð raðar				20181231 09:50:43
