helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:LB_DBFMT_FROM_USR\"\>Specifies a format from the list, if the format information of certain data fields is not accepted.\</ahelp\> The formats supplied here are only available for certain database fields, such as numeric or Boolean fields. If you select a database field in text format, you will not be able to select any format from the selection list, since the text format will be automatically maintained.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3144511				0	is	If the format you want is not listed, select "Other Formats..." and define the desired format in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Number Format\"\>\<emph\>Number Format\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154282				0	is	The number format assigned using the selection list always refers to the database field selected in the \<emph\>Database columns\</emph\> list box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	is	To insert the data into the document in the form of a table, the correct \<emph\>Table\</emph\> option must be active. You can then select a database field from the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box to define the formatting of the database field. The changes to the number formats will be applied to the last selection. It does not matter whether the database field was selected from the \<emph\>Database columns\</emph\> list box or from the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box.				20181231 09:50:43
