helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_FORMATTER\"\>Specifies that all field formats are considered when searching in the current document.\</ahelp\> Field formats are all visible formats that are created using the following possibilities:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	is	in table design mode for field properties,				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150488				0	is	in data source view on column formatting,				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152941				0	is	in forms on control properties.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156736				0	is	If the \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> box is marked, the data source view of the table or form is searched using the formatting set there. If the box is not marked, the database is searched using the formatting saved in the database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151280				0	is	Dæmi:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	is	You have a date field, which is saved in "DD.MM.YY" format in the database (for example, 17.02.65). The format of the entry is changed in the data source view to "DD MMM YYYY" (17 Feb 1965). Following this example, a record containing February 17 is only found when the \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> option is on:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150593				0	is	Virkja gagnasviðssnið				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145253				0	is	Search pattern				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3083279				0	is	virkt				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155850				0	is	"Feb" is returned, but not "2".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148590				0	is	óvirkt				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	is	"2" is returned, but not "Feb".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151321				0	is	It is recommended that you always search using field formatting.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149401				0	is	The following examples show possible issues when searching without field formatting. These issues depend on the database used and only occur for certain internal default formatting:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152971				0	is	Leitarniðurstöður				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154273				0	is	Stafsetur				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153836				0	is	"5" returns "14:00:00" as a time				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156332				0	is	Time fields are not defined for dBASE databases and must be simulated. To internally display the time "14:00:00", a 5 is necessary.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3157965				0	is	"00:00:00" returns all records of a standard date field				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146081				0	is	The database stores a date value internally using a combined date/time field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	is	"45.79" does not return "45.79" although the \<emph\>entire field\</emph\> option is selected under \<emph\>Position\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155518				0	is	The view shown does not match what is stored internally. For example, if value 45.789 is stored in the database as a field of type Number/Double and the shown formatting is set to display only two decimals, "45.79" is only returned in searches with field formatting.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148481				0	is	In this case, standard formatting is formatting that refers to the internally stored data. It is not always visible to the user, especially if it is used for simulating data types (for example, time fields in dBASE databases). This depends on the database used and the individual data type. Searching with field formatting is appropriate if you only want to find what is actually shown. This includes fields of type Date, Time, Date/Time and Number/Double.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507	31			0	is	However, searching without \<emph\>Apply field format \</emph\>is appropriate for larger databases with no formatting issues, because it is faster.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153355				0	is	If you are searching the values of check boxes, and \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> is on, then you will receive a "1" for marked check boxes, a "0" for unmarked check boxes, and an empty string for undefined (tristate) check boxes. If the search has been carried out with \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> set to off, you will see the language-dependent default values "TRUE" or "FALSE".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150995	119			0	is	If you use \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> when searching in list boxes, you find the text displayed in list boxes. If you do not use \<emph\>Apply field format,\</emph\> you will find the contents corresponding to the standard field format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150387				0	is	Passa við stafstöðu				20181231 09:50:43
