helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id6909390				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Applies all changes and closes the wizard.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147477				0	is	Tækjaslár				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149783				0	is	By clicking the arrow next to some icons you open a toolbar. To move a toolbar, drag the title bar. As soon as you release the mouse button, the toolbar remains at the new position. Drag the title bar to another position, or drag to an edge of the window, where the toolbar will dock. Close a toolbar by clicking the Close Window icon. Make the toolbar visible again by choosing \<emph\>View - Toolbars - (toolbar name)\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152414				0	is	Snúningshnappur				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id1094088				0	is	In form controls, a spin button is a property of a numerical field, currency field, date field, or time field. If the property "Spin button" is enabled, the field shows a pair of symbols with arrows pointing to opposing directions, either vertically or horizontally.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id7493209				0	is	In the Basic IDE, a spin button is the name used for the numerical field together with the two arrow symbols.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155599				0	is	You can type a numerical value into the field next to the spin button, or select the value with the up-arrow or down-arrow symbols on the spin button. On the keyboard you can press the up arrow and down arrow keys to increase or reduce the value. You can press the Page Up and Page Down keys to set the maximum and minimum value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150264				0	is	If the field next to the spin button defines numerical values, you can also define a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000003.xhp#metrik\" name=\"measurement unit\"\>measurement unit\</link\>, for example, 1 cm or 5 mm, 12 pt or 2".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154232				0	is	Umbreyta				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148983				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you click forward through the dialog, this button is called \<emph\>Next\</emph\>. On the last page the button has the name \<emph\>Convert\</emph\>. The conversion is then performed by clicking the button.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145129				0	is	Samhengisvalmynd				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156553				0	is	\<variable id=\"context\"\>To activate the context menu of an object, first click the object with the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>left\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> mouse button to select it, and then, \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>while holding down the Ctrl key or the Command and Option keys, click the mouse button again\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\> click the right mouse button\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. Some context menus can be called even if the object has not been selected. Context menus are found just about everywhere in $[officename].\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149180				0	is	Eyða				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Deletes the selected element or elements after confirmation.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147557				0	is	Eyða				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Deletes the selected element or elements without requiring confirmation.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148620				0	is	Einingar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	is	You can enter values in the input fields in different units of measurement. The default unit is inches. However, if you want a space of exactly 1cm, then type "1cm". Additional units are available according to the context, for example, 12 pt for a 12 point spacing. If the value of the new unit is unrealistic, the program uses a predefined maximum or minimum value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155535				0	is	Loka				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Closes the dialog and saves all changes.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275				0	is	Loka				20181231 09:50:43
