helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Almennar hugtakaskilgreiningar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154896				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>algeng hugtök;orðasöfn\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>orðasöfn;algeng hugtök\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>orðaskilgreiningar;almenn atriði\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154896				0	is	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp\" name=\"Almennar hugtakaskilgreiningar\"\>Almennar hugtakaskilgreiningar\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154788				0	is	Þessi orðalisti er til útskýringar á helstu hugtökum sem þú munt rekast á við notkun $[officename].				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154873				0	is	Notaðu orðasafnið til að fletta upp ókunnuglegum hugtökum sem þú gætir fundið í $[officename] forritunum.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156192				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>ASCII; skilgreining\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156192				0	is	ASCII				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	is	Abbreviation for American Standard Code for Information Interchange. ASCII is a character set for displaying fonts on personal computers. It consists of 128 characters including letters, numbers, punctuation and symbols. The extended ASCII character set contains 256 characters. Each character has been assigned a unique number, also referred to as ASCII Code.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150823				0	is	In HTML pages, only characters from the 7 Bit ASCII character set should appear. Other characters, such as German umlauts, are distinguished by way of a separate code. You can input extended ASCII code characters: the $[officename] export filter performs the necessary conversion.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151245				0	is	Bézier hlutur				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154924				0	is	Developed by the French mathematician Pierre Bézier, a Bézier curve is a mathematically defined curve used in two-dimensional graphic applications. The curve is defined by four points: the initial position and the terminating position, and two separate middle points. Bézier objects can be modified by moving these points with the mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146907				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>CTL;definition\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>flókin textaframsetning;skilgreining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>flókin textaframsetning, sjá CTL\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146907				0	is	Flókin textaframsetning (CTL)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3156081				0	is	Languages with complex text layout may have some or all of the following features:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116				0	is	The language is written with characters or glyphs that are composed of several parts				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154630				0	is	The text direction is from right to left.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3148677				0	is	Currently, $[officename] supports Hindi, Thai, Hebrew, and Arabic as CTL languages.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151176				0	is	Enable CTL support using \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_idN108F1				0	is	Samhengisvalmynd				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147084				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>DDE; skilgreining\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147084				0	is	DDE				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3145154				0	is	DDE stendur fyrir "Dynamic Data Exchange," sem er forveri OLE, "Object Linking and Embedding". Með DDE, eru hlutir tengdir í gegnum skráartilvísanir, en ekki innfellt.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154820				0	is	You can create a DDE link using the following procedure: Select cells from a Calc spreadsheet, copy them into the clipboard and switch to another spreadsheet and select the \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\> dialog. Select \<emph\>the Link\</emph\> option to insert the contents as a DDE link. When activating a link, the inserted cell area will be read from its original file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150439				0	is	Direct and Style Formatting				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3159254				0	is	If you format a document without Styles, it is referred to as "direct" formatting. This means modifying text or other objects, such as frames or tables, by applying various attributes directly. The format applies only to the selected area and all changes must be made separately. Styles, on the other hand, are not applied to the text directly, but rather are defined in the Styles and Formatting window and then applied. One advantage is that when you change a Style, all parts of the document to which that Style is assigned are modified at the same time.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287				0	is	You can remove direct formatting from your document by selecting the entire text with the shortcut keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A and then choosing \<emph\>Format - Default Formatting\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155132				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>windows; docking definition\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>docking; definition\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155132				0	is	Festing í glugga				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154638				0	is	\<variable id=\"andock1\"\>Some windows in $[officename], for example the Styles and Formatting window and the Navigator, are "dockable" windows. You can move these windows, re-size them or dock them to an edge. On each edge you can dock several windows on top of, or alongside each other; then, by moving the border lines, you can change the relative proportions of the windows.\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3147233				0	is	\<variable id=\"andock2\"\>To undock and re-dock, holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, double-click a vacant area in the window. In the Styles and Formatting window, you can also double-click a gray part of the window next to the icons, while you hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key.\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155306				0	is	Festing í glugga (Fela sjálfkrafa)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	is	On any window edge where another window is docked you will see a button which allows you to show or hide the window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3143274				0	is	If you click the button on the window edge to show the window, the window will remain visible until you manually hide it again (with the same button).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3153093				0	is	If you show the window by clicking the window border, but not the button, you activate the \<emph\>AutoHide\</emph\> function. The AutoHide function allows you to temporarily show a hidden window by clicking on its edge. When you click in the document, the docked window hides again.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163710				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>snið; skilgreining\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163710				0	is	Forsníðing				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3163821				0	is	Formatting refers to the visual layout of text using a word-processing or DTP program. This includes defining the paper format, page borders, fonts and font effects, as well as indents and spacing. You can format text \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#Section7\"\>directly or with Styles\</link\> provided by $[officename].				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156006				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>IME; skilgreining\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156006				0	is	IME				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3157874				0	is	IME stands for Input Method Editor. A program that allows the user to enter complex characters from non-western character sets using a standard keyboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151172				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>JDBC; skilgreining\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151172				0	is	JDBC				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3148386				0	is	Hægt er að nota Java Database Connectivity (JDBC) API til að tengjast við gagnagrunn frá %PRODUCTNAME. JDBC reklar eru skrifaðir í Java forritunarmálinu og eru óháðir stýrikerfi.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151282				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>stafþjöppun; skilgreining\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151282				0	is	Stafþjöppun				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3146321				0	is	Stafþjöppun (kerning) er þegar bil á milli stafapara er aukið eða minnkað til þess að bæta heildarásýnd texta og gera hann auðlæsilegri.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3146078				0	is	Stafþjöppunartöflur (kerning tables) innihalda upplýsingar um hvaða stafapör þurfi meira millibil en önnur. Slíkar stafþjöppunartöflur eru venjulega hluti af leturskrám.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150592				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>tenglar; skilgreining\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150592				0	is	Tengill				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150092				0	is	The \<emph\>Links\</emph\> command is found in the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> menu. The command can only be activated when at least one link is contained in the current document. When you insert a picture, for example, you can either insert the picture directly into the document or insert the picture as a link.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3145730				0	is	When an object is inserted directly into a document, the document size increases by (at least) the size in bytes of the object. You can save the document and open it on another computer, and the inserted object will still be in the same position in the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3144765				0	is	If you insert the object as a link, only a reference to the file name is inserted. The file size of the document increases only by the path and file reference. If you open your document on another computer, however, the linked file must be in exactly the same position as given by the reference in order to view the object in the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3153334				0	is	Use \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\> to see which files are inserted as links. The links can be removed if required. This will break the link and insert the object directly.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154512				0	is	Talningarkerfi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3157846				0	is	A number system is determined by the number of characters available for representing numbers. The decimal system, for instance is based on the ten numbers (0..9), the binary system is based on the two numbers 0 and 1, the hexadecimal system is based on 16 characters (0...9 and A...F).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156358				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>hlutir; skilgreining\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156358				0	is	Object				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3144748				0	is	An object is a screen element containing data. It can refer to application data, such as text or graphics.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3153839				0	is	Objects are independent and do not influence each other. Any object containing data can be assigned certain commands. For example, a graphic object has commands for image editing and a spreadsheet contains calculation commands.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152827				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>ODBC; skilgreining\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152827				0	is	ODBC				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3153530				0	is	Open Database Connectivity (ODBC) is a protocol norm with which applications can access database systems. The query language used is Structured Query Language (SQL). In $[officename], you can determine for each database whether to use SQL commands to run queries. Alternatively, you can use the interactive help to define your query by mouseclick and have it automatically translated into SQL by $[officename].				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3153956				0	is	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>The 32bit ODBC functions required here can be installed on your system at any time with the help of the setup program supplied with your database. You can then amend the properties through the Control Panel. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154479				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>OLE; skilgreining\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154479				0	is	OLE				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3157840				0	is	Object Linking and Embedding (OLE) objects can be linked to a target document or may also be embedded. Embedding inserts a copy of the object and details of the source program in the target document. If you want to edit the object, simply activate the source program by double-clicking on the object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154507				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>OpenGL; skilgreining\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154507				0	is	OpenGL				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3146879				0	is	OpenGL represents a 3D graphics language, initially developed by SGI (Silicon Graphics Inc). Two dialects of this language are commonly used: Microsoft OpenGL, developed for use under Windows NT, and Cosmo OpenGL made by SGI. The latter represents an independent graphics language for all platforms and all kind of computers, even usable on machines without special 3-D graphics hardware.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155764				0	is	PNG				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3148993				0	is	Portable Network Graphics (PNG) er grafískt skráarsnið. Skrárnar eru þjappaðar með valkvæmu þjöppunargildi, og, ólíkt JPG myndum, eru PNG skrár alltaf þjappaðar án þess að neinar upplýsingar tapist.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083286				0	is	Aðallykill				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150323				0	is	A primary key serves as a unique identifier of database fields. The unique identification of database fields is used in \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#relational\"\>relational databases\</link\>, to access data in other tables. If reference is made to a primary key from another table, this is termed a foreign key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3148916				0	is	In $[officename], you define the primary key in the design view of a table, by choosing the relevant command from the context menu of a row header for the selected field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147359				0	is	Venslaður gagnagrunnur				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3147585	101			0	is	Venslaður gagnagrunnur er samasafn af gögnum sem eru tengdar saman með formlegum töfluskilgreiningum þar sem hægt er að nálgast gögnin og tengja saman á marga vegu án þess að það þurfi að endurhanna töflurnar. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	is	Venslað gagnagrunnskerfi (RDBMS) er forrit sem gerir þér kleyft að búa til, uppfæra, og sýsla með venslaða gagnagrunn. RDMBS notar Structured Query Language (SQL) skipanir sem eru slegnar inn frá notanda eða eru innbyggðar í forrit og þessar skipanir búa til, uppfæra, eða gefa aðgang að gagnagrunninum.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3147535				0	is	A good example of a relational database can be given with a database containing Customer, Purchase, and Invoice tables. In the Invoice table, there is no actual customer or purchasing data; however, the table contains references through a relational link, or a relation, to the respective customer and purchasing table's fields (for example, the customer ID field from the customer table).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147315				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>afstillt á síðu; skilgreining\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147315				0	is	Afstillt á síðu				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154223				0	is	Afstillt á síðu (Register-true) er hugtak sem er notað í letursetningu og prentun. Hugtakið vísar til þess að leturlínur á fram- og bakhliðum hverrar síðu eru stilltar af til að þær falli saman, algeng notkun er við prentun bóka, dagblaða og tímarita. Afstilling á síðu gerir það að verkum að skuggar frá stöfum á bakhliðinni lenda í línunum á þeirri sem snýr fram (en ekki á milli lína) og verður texti þar með mun auðveldari aflestrar. Hugtakið á líka við um það þegar línur í aðliggjandi dálkum eru þvingaðar til að standast á og fá sömu hæð.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3145230				0	is	Þegar þú skilgreinir málsgrein, málsgreinarstíl eða síðustíl sem afstillt á síðu (register-true), þá eru grunnlínur viðkomandi stafa stilltar miðað við ákveðin lóðrétt hnit, óháð leturstærð eða nálægð við myndefni. Ef þú vilt, þá geturðu tilgreint eiginleika þessa hnitanets sem eigindi síðustíls.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156710				0	is	RTF				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151186				0	is	Rich Text Format (RTF) er skráarsnið sem var hannað til að skiptast á textaskrám. Sérstakur eiginleiki sniðsins er að sniðum er breytt beint í lesanlegt textasnið. Því miður, í samanburði við önnur skáaarsnið, býr þetta til frekar stórar skrár.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156372				0	is	Saving Relatively and Absolutely				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3146919				0	is	In various dialogs (for example, \<emph\>Edit - AutoText\</emph\>) you can select whether you want to save files relatively or absolutely.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3152946				0	is	If you choose to save relatively, the references to embedded graphics or other objects in your document will be saved relative to the location in the file system. In this case, it does not matter where the referenced directory structure is recorded. The files will be found regardless of location, as long as the reference remains on the same drive or volume. This is important if you want to make the document available to other computers that may have a completely different directory structure, drive or volume names. It is also recommended to save relatively if you want to create a directory structure on an Internet server.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3148927				0	is	If you prefer absolute saving, all references to other files will also be defined as absolute, based on the respective drive, volume or root directory. The advantage is that the document containing the references can be moved to other directories or folders, and the references remain valid.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149922				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>SQL;skilgreining\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149922				0	is	SQL				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3152863				0	is	Structured Query Language (SQL) is a language used for database queries. In $[officename] you can formulate queries either in SQL or interactively with the mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147552				0	is	SQL gagnagrunnur / SQL miðlari				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3159239				0	is	An SQL database is a database system which offers an \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#sql\"\>SQL\</link\> interface. SQL databases are often used in client/server networks in which different clients access a central server (for example, an SQL server), hence they are also called SQL server databases, or SQL servers for short.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3159118				0	is	In $[officename], you can integrate external SQL databases. These may be located on your local hard disk as well as on the network. Access is achieved through \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#odbc\"\>ODBC\</link\>, JDBC, or a native driver integrated into $[officename].				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166423				0	is	Einstæðingar og munaðarleysingjar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149448				0	is	Einstæðingar og munaðarleysingjar (widow / orphan) eru hugtök úr setjaraiðn sem eiga sér langa sögu. Með einstæðingi er átt við stutta línu í enda málsgreinar, sem við prentun endar stök efst á næstu síðu. Munaðarleysingi er aftur á móti þar sem fyrsta lína í málsgrein lendir neðst á síðunni á undan megintexta málsgreinarinnar. Í textaskjölum $[officename] geturðu komið í veg fyrir að þetta tvennt geti gerst, og er það stillt í málsgreinastílum. Við að stilla þetta, þarf að tilgreina lágmarksfjölda lína sem á að halda saman á blaðsíðu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000206.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Dif Import/Export/ Lotus import/ dBASE import				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000206.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155354				0	is	Dif Import/Export/ Lotus import/ dBASE import				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000206.xhp	0	help	par_id3150620				0	is	Defines the options for import/export. These dialogs will be automatically shown if the corresponding file type is selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000206.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149000				0	is	Stafatafla				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000206.xhp	0	help	par_id3152790				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_IMPORTOPT:LB_FONT\"\>Select the character set from the options used for import/export.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000206.xhp	0	help	par_id3152942				0	is	For further information regarding filters, refer to the topic: \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000020.xhp\" name=\"Information about Import and Export Filters\"\>Information about Import and Export Filters\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
