helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id314995711				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>When this option is enabled, fields or cells whose values are quoted in their entirety (the first and last characters of the value equal the text delimiter) are imported as text.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	hd_id314847422				0	is	Uppgötva sérstakar tölur				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id314995722				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>When this option is enabled, Calc will automatically detect all number formats, including special number formats such as dates, time, and scientific notation.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id314995723				0	is	The selected language influences how such special numbers are detected, since different languages and regions many have different conventions for such special numbers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id314995724				0	en-US	When this option is disabled, Calc will detect and convert only decimal numbers. The rest, including numbers formatted in scientific notation, will be imported as text. A decimal number string can have digits 0-9, thousands separators, and a decimal separator. Thousands separators and decimal separators may vary with the selected language and region.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3149957				0	en-US	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_ASCII:LB_TYPE1\"\>Choose a column in the preview window and select the data type to be applied the imported data.\</ahelp\> You can select one of the following options:				20181231 09:50:43
