helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\01110200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151054				0	is	WebCast				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\01110200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150543				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"SD:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_PUBLISHING:PAGE2_WEBCAST\"\>In a WebCast export, automatic scripts will be generated with Perl or ASP support.\</ahelp\> This enables the speaker (for example, a speaker in a telephone conference using a slide show on the Internet) to change the slides in the audience's web browsers. You will find more information on \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01110200.xhp\" name=\"WebCast\"\>WebCast\</link\> later in this section.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\01110200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154365				0	is	Active Server Pages (ASP)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\01110200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148922	28			0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"SD:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_PUBLISHING:PAGE2_ASP\"\>When you select the\<emph\> ASP \</emph\>option, the WebCast export creates ASP pages. Note that the HTML presentation can only be offered by a web server supporting ASP.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
