helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	is	This section contains information about how to create a new database table in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05010000.xhp\" name=\"design view\"\>design view\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154288				0	is	Open the database file of the database where you want a new table. Click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon. Choose \<emph\>Create Table in Design View\</emph\> to create a new table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798				0	is	In the Design view, you can now create the fields for your table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3153349				0	is	Enter new fields in rows from top to bottom. Click the \<emph\>Field Name\</emph\> cell and enter a field name for each data field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id1595507				0	is	Include a "primary key" data field. Base needs a primary key to be able to edit the table contents. A primary key has unique contents for each data record. For example, insert a numerical field, right-click the first column, and choose \<emph\>Primary Key\</emph\> from the context menu. Set \<emph\>AutoValue\</emph\> to "Yes", so Base can automatically increment the value for each new record.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	is	In the next cell to the right, define the \<emph\>Field Type\</emph\>. When you click in the cell, you can select a field type in the combo box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	is	Each field can only accept data corresponding to the specified field type. For example, it is not possible to enter text in a number field. Memo fields in dBASE III format are references to internally-managed text files which can hold up to 64KB text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	is	You can enter an optional \<emph\>Description\</emph\> for each field. The text of the description will appear as a tip on the column headings in the table view.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153379				0	is	Eiginleikar svæðis				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	is	Enter properties for each selected data field. Depending on the database type, some input facilities may not be available.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	is	In the \<emph\>Default value\</emph\> box, enter the default contents for every new record. This contents can be edited later.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	is	In the \<emph\>Entry required\</emph\> box, specify whether or not the field may remain empty.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	is	For the \<emph\>Length\</emph\> box, a combo box may be shown that provides the available choices.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; copying areas to text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; sheet areas, to text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;sheet areas in text documents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927				0	is	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_table.xhp\" name=\"Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\"\>Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	is	Open both the text document and the spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	is	Select the sheet area you want to copy.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149827				0	is	Point to the selected area and press the mouse button. Keep the mouse button pressed for a moment, then drag the area into the text document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780	32			0	is	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible next to each other, first drag the mouse pointer to the destination document button. Continue to hold down the mouse button. The document is displayed, and you can move the mouse pointer within the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	is	Once the cursor is located in the place where you want to insert the sheet area, release the mouse button. The sheet area is inserted as an OLE object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154047				0	is	You can select and edit the OLE object at any time.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	is	To edit the OLE object, double-click on it.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155389				0	is	Alternatively, select the object and choose \<emph\>Edit - Object - Edit\</emph\> or choose \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> from the context menu. You edit the object in its own frame within the text document, but you see the icons and menu commands needed for spreadsheets.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	is	Choose \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to open the source document of the OLE object.				20181231 09:50:43
