helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10743				0	is	Contents that are stored on the clipboard can be pasted into your document using different formats. In %PRODUCTNAME you can choose how to paste the contents using a dialog or a drop-down icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10746				0	is	The available options depend on the contents of the clipboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144547360				0	is	In Writer text documents, you can press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+V to paste the contents of the clipboard as unformatted text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	is	Pasting clipboard contents using an icon menu				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10750				0	is	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Paste\</emph\> icon on the Standard Bar to open the menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10758				0	is	Select one of the options.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075B				0	is	If you do not like the result, click the \<emph\>Undo\</emph\> icon and then paste again with another option.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10762				0	is	Pasting clipboard contents using a dialog				20181231 09:50:43
