helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	is	If you want to exchange data with a database that does not have an ODBC link and does not allow dBASE import and export, you can use a common text format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145313				0	is	Importing Data into $[officename]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	is	To exchange data in a text format use the $[officename] Calc import/export filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	is	Export the desired data from the source database in a text format. The CSV text format is recommended. This format separates data fields by using delimiters such as commas or semi-colons, and separates records by inserting line breaks.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	is	Choose \<emph\>File - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>\<emph\>Open\</emph\>\</link\> and click the file to import.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id1977904				0	is	Select "Text CSV" from the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> combo box. Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	is	The \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Text Import\"\>\<emph\>Text Import\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears. Decide which data to include from the text document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986				0	is	Once the data is in a $[officename] Calc spreadsheet, you can edit it as needed. Save the data as a $[officename] data source:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	is	Save the current $[officename] Calc spreadsheet in dBASE format in the folder of a dBASE database. To do this, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>, then select the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> "dBASE" and the folder of the dBASE database.				20181231 09:50:43
