helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	is	You can export the current $[officename] spreadsheet in a text format which can be read by many other applications.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	is	Veldu \<emph\>Skrá - Vista sem\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154216				0	is	In \<emph\>File type\</emph\> select the filter "Text CSV". Enter a file name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	is	This opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"dBase Export\"\>\<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, in which you can select the character set, field delimiter and text delimiter. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. A warning informs you that only the active sheet was saved.				20181231 09:50:43
