helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	is	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. The \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page of the dialog opens.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	is	Click on \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>. This opens the Properties dialog for your printer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3145313				0	is	Select the option to print in black and white. For further information, refer to the user's manual of your printer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	is	Confirm the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog and click \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	is	The current document will be printed in black and white.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147653				0	is	Printing in black and white in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Impress and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	is	Choose Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress or Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Draw, as appropriate.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	is	Then choose \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573	12			0	is	Under \<emph\>Quality,\</emph\> select either \<emph\>Grayscale\</emph\> or \<emph\>Black & white\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154307				0	is	When either of these options is selected, all presentations or drawings will be printed without color. If you only want to print in black for the \<emph\>current\</emph\> print job, select the option in \<emph\>File - Print - %PRODUCTNAME Draw/Impress\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149786	15			0	is	               \<emph\>Grayscale\</emph\> converts all colors to a maximum of 256 gradations from black to white. All text will be printed in black. A background set by \<emph\>Format - Page - Background\</emph\> will not be printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610	16			0	is	               \<emph\>Black & white\</emph\> converts all colors into the two values black and white. All borders around objects are printed black. All text will be printed in black. A background set by \<emph\>Format - Page - Background\</emph\> will not be printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	is	Printing only text in black and white				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147559				0	is	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer you can choose to print color-formatted text in black and white. You can specify this either for all subsequent text documents to be printed, or only for the current printing process.				20181231 09:50:43
