helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id2659077				0	is	Útgáfa ODF-sniðs				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id6944181				0	is	OpenOffice.org 3 and StarOffice 9 introduce new features which have to be saved using the \<link href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenDocument\"\>OpenDocument\</link\> format (ODF) version 1.2. The prior versions of OpenOffice.org 2 and StarOffice 8 support the file formats ODF 1.0/1.1. Those prior file formats cannot store all new features of the new software.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id886257				0	is	Current versions can open documents in ODF formats 1.0/1.1 and 1.2.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id8892483				0	is	When you save a document, you can select whether to save the document in the format ODF 1.2, ODF 1.2 (Extended), or in the prior format ODF 1.0/1.1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id0915200911205367				0	is	Currently, the ODF 1.2 (Extended) format enables files of Draw and Impress to contain comments. Those comments can be inserted by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Comment\</item\> in the latest software version. The comments get lost when loading files into prior software versions that were saved by the latest software version.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id7198400				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Some companies or organizations may require ODF documents in the ODF 1.0/1.1 format. You can select that format to save in the listbox. This older format cannot store all new features, so the new format ODF 1.2 (Extended) is recommended where possible.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164920				0	is	File encryption algorithm for ODF 1.2 format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3160488	78			0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SFXPAGE_SAVE_BTN_ODFENCRYPTION\"\>Change the default file encryption from blowfish to AES-256 when ODF 1.2 is used.\</ahelp\> The default file encryption algorithm is blowfish but when ODF 1.2 is used the user can change the default to AES-256. Older encrypted documents can still be loaded but new encrypted documents can't be opened with older office versions. The AES-256 algorithm is more secure than blowfish.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154920				0	is	Besta stærð fyrir ODF-skráasnið				20181231 09:50:43
