helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152777				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE_CB_TAB_ALIGNMENT\"\>Specifies how to align text at tab stops beyond the right margin, how to handle decimal tab stops, and how to handle tab stops close to a line break.\</ahelp\> If this check box is not selected, tab stops are handled in the same way as in other Office applications.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10810				0	is	In text documents created by your current version of Writer, the new tab stop handling is used by default. In text documents created by Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, the old tab stop handling is applied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F9				0	is	Ekki auka línubil milli textalína				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10806				0	is	Specifies that additional leading (extra space) between lines of text is not added, even if the font in use contains the additional leading attribute.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10809				0	is	In text documents created by your current version of Writer, the additional leading is used by default. In text documents created by Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, the additional leading is not used.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FF				0	is	Use %WRITERCOMPATIBILITYVERSIONOOO11 line spacing				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10815				0	is	If the option is off, a new process for formatting text lines with proportional line spacing will be applied. If the option is on, the previous method of formatting of text lines with proportional line spacing will be applied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10818				0	is	In text documents created by your current version of Writer and in Microsoft Word documents of recent versions, the new process is used. In text documents created by Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, the previous process is used.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081B				0	is	Bæta við málsgreina- og töflubilum neðst í töflureitum				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10846				0	is	Specifies that the bottom spacing is added to a paragraph, even when it is the last paragraph in a table cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10849				0	is	If the option is off, table cells will be formatted as in Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0. If the option is on, an alternative method of formatting table cells will be applied. The option is on by default for new documents created with %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION and for documents imported from Microsoft Word format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084C				0	is	Use %WRITERCOMPATIBILITYVERSIONOOO11 object positioning				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10864				0	is	Specifies how to calculate the position of floating objects anchored to a character or paragraph with respect to the top and bottom paragraph spacing.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10867				0	is	If the option is on, the floating objects are positioned as in Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0. If the option is off, the floating objects are positioned using an alternative method that is similar to the method used by Microsoft Word. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1086A				0	is	The option will be set to off for new documents. For Writer documents created by a version prior to %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION the option is on.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10821				0	is	Use %WRITERCOMPATIBILITYVERSIONOOO11 text wrapping around objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id4016541				0	is	MS Word and Writer have different approaches on wrapping text around floating screen objects. Floating screen object are Writer frames and drawing objects, and the objects 'text box', 'graphic', 'frame', 'picture' etc. in MS Word.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id7280190				0	is	In MS Word and in current versions of Writer, page header/footer content and footnote/endnote content does not wrap around floating screen objects. Text body content wraps around floating screen objects which are anchored in the page header. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id2782982				0	is	In Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, the opposite was true.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10892				0	is	If the option is off, which is the default setting, the new text wrapping will be applied. If the option is on, the former text wrapping will be applied. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1092A				0	is	Taka tillit til gerðar textaskriðs þegar hlutir eru staðsettir				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	is	Specifies how the complex process of positioning floating objects that are anchored to a character or paragraph should work. In Writer versions prior to StarOffice 8 or OpenOffice.org 2.0, an iterative process was used, while in current versions a straightforward process is used, which is similar to the same process in Microsoft Word.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10943				0	is	If the option is off, the old %PRODUCTNAME iterative process of object positioning is used. If the option is on, the new straightforward process is used to ensure compatibility with Microsoft Word documents.				20181231 09:50:43
