helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	HTML import and export				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154380				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>importing; HTML with META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; to HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML; importing META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; META tags in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tags; META tags\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154380				0	is	HTML import and export				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	is	When you export a file to an HTML document, the description and the user-defined file properties are included as META \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#tags\" name=\"tags\"\>tags\</link\> between the HEAD tags of the exported document. META tags are not displayed in a Web browser, and are used to include information, such as keywords for search engines on your Web page. To set the properties of the current document, choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Description\</emph\> or \<emph\>User Defined\</emph\> tabs, and then type the information you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	is	The following file properties are converted to META tags when you export a file as an HTML document:				20181231 09:50:43
