helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC2				0	is	To change the color of a text selection, select the text that you want to change, and click the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon. To apply a different color, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon, and then select the color that you want to use.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC9				0	is	If you click the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon before you select text, the paint can cursor appears. To change the color of text, select the text with the paint can cursor. To change the color of a single word, double-click in a word. To apply a different color, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon, and then select the color that you want to use.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CD6				0	is	To undo the last change, right-click.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CDA				0	is	To exit the paint can mode, click once, or press the Escape key.				20181231 09:50:43
