helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154836				0	is	Including Text in Number Format Codes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398				0	is	Text and Numbers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3154224				0	is	To include text in a number format that is applied to a cell containing numbers, place a double quotation mark (") in front of and behind the text, or a backslash (\\) before a single character. For example, enter \<emph\>#.# "meters"\</emph\> to display "3.5 meters" or \<emph\>#.# \\m\</emph\> to display "3.5 m".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148979				0	is	Text and Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153338				0	is	To include text in a number format that is applied to a cell that might contain text, enclose the text by double quotation marks (" "), and then add an at sign (@). For example, enter \<emph\>"Total for "@\</emph\> to display "Total for December".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154330				0	is	Bil				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3156294				0	is	To use a character to define the width of a space in a number format, type an underscore ( _ ) followed by the character. The width of the space varies according to the width of the character that you choose. For example, \<emph\>_M\</emph\> creates a wider space than \<emph\>_i\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155994				0	is	Litur				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423				0	is	To set the color of a section of a number format code, insert one of the following color names in square brackets [ ]:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3154630				0	is	BLÁGRÆNN				20181231 09:50:43
