helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154073				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_RADIOBUTTON_DLG_REL_PROPERTIES_RB_CASC_UPD\"\>Updates all the external key fields if the value of the corresponding primary key has been modified (Cascading Update).\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145171				0	is	Setja sem null				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_RADIOBUTTON_DLG_REL_PROPERTIES_RB_CASC_UPD_NULL\"\> If the corresponding primary key has been modified, use this option to set the "IS NULL" value to all external key fields. IS NULL means that the field is empty.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150448				0	is	Gera sjálfgefið				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_RADIOBUTTON_DLG_REL_PROPERTIES_RB_CASC_UPD_DEFAULT\"\> If the corresponding primary key has been modified, use this option to set a default value to all external key fields.\</ahelp\> During the creation of the corresponding table, the default value of an external key field will be defined when you assign the field properties.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	is	Valkostir eyðingar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153193				0	is	Here you can select options that take effect when a primary key field is deleted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159252				0	is	Engin aðgerð				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_RADIOBUTTON_DLG_REL_PROPERTIES_RB_NO_CASC_DEL\"\>Specifies that the deletion of a primary key will not have any effect on other external key fields.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154146				0	is	Eyða keðjuverkun				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155309				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_RADIOBUTTON_DLG_REL_PROPERTIES_RB_CASC_DEL\"\>Specifies that all external key fields will be deleted if you delete the corresponding primary key field.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153140	22			0	is	When you delete a primary key field with the\<emph\> Delete cascade \</emph\>option, all records from other tables that have this key as their foreign key are also deleted. Use this option with great care; it is possible that a major portion of the database can be deleted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	is	Setja sem null				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_RADIOBUTTON_DLG_REL_PROPERTIES_RB_CASC_DEL_NULL\"\>If you delete the corresponding primary key, the "IS NULL" value will be assigned to all external key fields.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145272				0	is	Gera sjálfgefið				20181231 09:50:43
