helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146957				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>relational databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957	2			0	is	This command opens the \<emph\>Relation Design \</emph\>window, which allows you to define relationships between various database tables.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CTL_RELATIONTAB\"\>Here you can link together tables from the current database through common data fields.\</ahelp\> Click the \<emph\>New Relation\</emph\> icon to create the relationships, or simply drag-and-drop with the mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145316				0	is	This function is only available if you are working with a relational database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149235				0	is	When you choose \<emph\>Tools - Relationships\</emph\>, a window opens in which all the existing relationships between the tables of the current database are shown. If no relationships have been defined, or if you want to relate other tables of the database to each other, then click the \<emph\>Add Tables\</emph\> icon. The \<link href=\"text/shared/02/14020100.xhp\" name=\"Add Tables\"\>Add Tables\</link\> dialog opens in which you can select the tables that you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152812				0	is	If the \<emph\>Relation Design\</emph\> window is open, the selected tables cannot be modified, even in Table Design mode. This ensures that tables are not changed while the relations are being created.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	is	The selected tables are shown in the top area of the design view. You can close a table window through the context menu or with the Delete key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148922				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>primary keys;inserting (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keys;primary keys (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>external keys (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148922				0	is	Primary key and other key				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149168				0	is	If you want to define a relation among the different tables, you should enter a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#primaerschluessel\" name=\"primary key\"\>primary key\</link\> that clearly identifies a data field of the existing table. You can refer to the primary key from other tables to access the data of this table. All data fields referring to this primary key will be identified as an external key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147085				0	is	All data fields referring to a primary key will be identified in the table window by a small key symbol.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153193				0	is	Define relations				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155430				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>relations; creating and deleting (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155430				0	is	All existing relations are shown in the relations windows by a line that connects the primary and other key fields. You can add a relation by using drag-and-drop to drop the field of one table onto the field of the other table. A relation is removed again by selecting it and pressing the Delete key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149984				0	is	Alternatively, you can also click the \<emph\>New Relation\</emph\> icon in the top area of the relation field and define the relation between two tables in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Relations\"\>\<emph\>Relations\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153093				0	is	If you use $[officename] as the front-end for a relational database, the creation and deletion of relationships is not placed in an intermediate memory by $[officename], but is forwarded directly to the external database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155856	15			0	is	By double-clicking a connection line, you can assign certain properties to the relation. The \<emph\>Relations \</emph\>dialog opens.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaprop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Eiginleikar gagnagrunns				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaprop.xhp	0	help	par_idN10550				0	is	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabaprop.xhp\"\>Eiginleikar gagnagrunns\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaprop.xhp	0	help	par_idN10560				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the properties of a database.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaprop.xhp	0	help	par_id1322977				0	is	In a database window, choose \<emph\>Edit - Database - Properties\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Eiginleikar tengingar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154015				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>links;relational databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inner joins (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>joins in databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>left joins (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>right joins (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>full joins (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154015				0	is	Eiginleikar tengingar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151205				0	is	If you double-click a connection between two linked fields in the query design, or if you choose \<emph\>Insert - New Relation\</emph\>, the \<emph\>Join Properties\</emph\> dialog appears. These properties will be used in all queries created in the future.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155066				0	is	Töflur sem koma við sögu				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153924				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_RIGHT_TABLE\"\>Specifies two different tables that you want to join.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	is	Svið sem koma við sögu				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148994				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies two data fields that will be joined by a relation.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159267				0	is	Valkostir				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147340				0	is	Tegund				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152482				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>Specifies the link type of the selected link.\</ahelp\> Some databases support only a subset of the possible types.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155334				0	is	Innri töflutenging				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155936				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>With the internal join, the results table contains only the records for which the content of the linked fields is the same.\</ahelp\> In $[officename] SQL this type of link is created by a corresponding WHERE clause.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156372				0	is	Vinstri töflutenging				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3166450				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>With the left join, the results table contains all fields of the left table and only those fields of the right table for which the content of the linked fields is the same.\</ahelp\> In $[officename] SQL this type of link corresponds to the LEFT OUTER JOIN command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155607				0	is	Hægri töflutenging				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150647				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>With the right join, the results table contains all fields of the right table and only those fields of the left table for which the content of the linked fields is the same.\</ahelp\> In $[officename] SQL this type of link corresponds to the RIGHT OUTER JOIN command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158215				0	is	Full Join				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3163665				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>For a full join, the results table contains all fields of the left and right tables.\</ahelp\> In the SQL of $[officename] this type of link corresponds to the FULL OUTER JOIN command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200912031976				0	is	Náttúruleg				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200912031977				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Inserts the keyword NATURAL into the SQL statement that defines the relation. The relation joins all columns that have the same column name in both tables. The resulting joined table contains only one column for each pair of equally named columns.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Hópun og röðun				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	hd_id3486434				0	is	\<variable id=\"rep_sort\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_sort.xhp\"\>Hópun og röðun\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3068636				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>In the Sorting and Grouping dialog of \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\>, you can define the fields that should be sorted in your report, and the fields that should be kept together to form a group.\</ahelp\> If you group your report by a certain field, all records with the same value of that field will be kept together in one group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id876186				0	is	The Groups box shows the fields in an order from top to bottom. You can select any field, then click the Move Up or Move Down button to move this field up or down in the list. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3939634				0	is	The sorting and grouping will be applied in the order of the list from top to bottom.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id599688				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Lists the fields that will be used for sorting or grouping. The field at the top has the highest priority, the second field has the second priority, and so on.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id1371501				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to open a list from which you can select a field.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id4661702				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves the selected field up in the list.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7868892				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves the selected field down in the list.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id2188787				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the sorting order.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id5833307				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select to show or hide the Group Header.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7726676				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select to show or hide the Group Footer.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3729361				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select to create a new group on each changed value, or on other properties.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200922142041				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Removes the selected field from the list.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3405560				0	is	By default a new group is created on every changed value of a record from the selected field. You can change this property depending on the type of field:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3409527				0	is	For fields of type Text, you can select Prefix Characters and enter a number n of characters in the text box below. The records which are identical in the first n characters will be grouped together.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7112338				0	is	For fields of type Date/Time, you can group the records by the same year, quarter, month, week, day, hour, or minute. You can additionally specify an interval for weeks and hours: 2 weeks groups data in biweekly groups, 12 hours groups data in half-day groups.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id2855616				0	is	For fields of type AutoNumber, Currency, or Number, you specify an interval.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7700430				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the group interval value that records are grouped by.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id1180455				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the level of detail by which a group is kept together on the same page.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id2091433				0	is	When you specify to keep together some records on the same page, you have three choices:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id5092318				0	is	No - page boundaries are not taken into account.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id9312417				0	is	Whole Group - prints the group header, detail section, and group footer on the same page.				20181231 09:50:43
