helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155962				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>text strings; entering in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>direct text; entering in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;text in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	hd_id5676442				0	is	\<variable id=\"text\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/text.xhp\" name=\"Innsláttur texta\"\>Innsláttur texta\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	hd_id8509170				0	is	How to enter direct text strings that do not get interpreted?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_id337229				0	is	Some text strings get interpreted as operators automatically. Sometimes this is not what you want. If you want to write W\<emph\>*\</emph\> (a letter with a superscripted asterisk), the asterisk will be interpreted as a multiplication operator. Enclose the direct text within double quotes or add spaceholders.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D0				0	is	Dæmi:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_id521866				0	is	An imported MathType formula contains the following string				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_id9413739				0	is	W rSup { size 8{*} }				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_id755943				0	is	If you have set up Math to convert imported MathType formulas (in \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - Microsoft Office), you see the formula with a placeholder instead of the asterisk.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_id5988952				0	is	Change {*} to {} * {} as in the following formula:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_id3304544				0	is	W rSup { size 8{} * {} }				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_id4941557				0	is	You can also use W^"*" to enter the character as direct text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\text.xhp	0	help	par_id9961851				0	is	Some formulas start with an = sign. Use "=" to enter that character as direct text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Manually Aligning Formula Parts				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156384				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>aligning; characters in %PRODUCTNAME Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula parts; manually aligning\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156384				0	is	\<variable id=\"align\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/align.xhp\" name=\"Manually Aligning Formula Parts\"\>Manually Aligning Formula Parts\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154657				0	is	How do you align characters in $[officename] Math quickly and easily?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	par_id3150249				0	is	To accomplish this, you must define empty groups and character strings. They do not require any space, but carry information that helps in the alignment process.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	par_id3153912				0	is	To create empty groups, enter curly brackets \<emph\>{}\</emph\> in the Commands window. In the following example, the goal is to achieve a line break so that the plus signs are beneath one another, even though one less character is entered in the upper line:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	par_id3153246				0	is	a+a+a+{} newline {}{}{}{}{}a+a+a+a				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	par_id3143229				0	is	Empty character strings are a simple way to ensure that texts and formulas are left-aligned. They are defined using double inverted commas "" . Make sure you do not use any typographic inverted commas. Example:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	par_id3153809				0	is	"A further example." newline a+b newline ""c-d				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Merging Formula Parts in Brackets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152596				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>brackets; merging formula parts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula parts; merging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fractions in formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging;formula parts\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	is	\<variable id=\"brackets\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/brackets.xhp\" name=\"Merging Formula Parts in Brackets\"\>Merging Formula Parts in Brackets\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154511				0	is	Inserting fractions into formulas				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3146971				0	is	In the case of a fraction whose numerator and denominator consist of a product, a sum, and so on, the values that belong together must be bracketed together.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3149021				0	is	Use the following syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3083280				0	is	{a + c} over 2 = m				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3154703				0	is	or				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3150297				0	is	m = {a + c} over 2				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Entering Comments				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155961				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>comments; entering in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;comments in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155961				0	is	\<variable id=\"comment\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/comment.xhp\" name=\"Entering Comments\"\>Entering Comments\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154657				0	is	How does one attach comments that don't appear in the document to a formula?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	par_id3149499				0	is	A comment begins with a double percent sign \<emph\>%%\</emph\>, and extends to the next line-end character (Enter key). Everything that lies in between is ignored and is not printed out. If there are percent signs in the text, they are treated as part of the text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D0				0	is	Dæmi:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D3				0	is	a^2+b^2=c^2 %% Pythagorean theorem.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\main.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Leiðbeiningar fyrir notkun $[officename] Math				20181231 09:50:43
