helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	hd_id1892147				0	is	\<variable id=\"limits\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/limits.xhp\"\>Working with Limits\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	hd_id9881893				0	is	How can I define the limits in a Sum or Integral formula?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id6504409				0	is	You want to insert a summation formula like "summation of s^k from k = 0 to n" at the cursor in a Writer text document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id8811304				0	is	Veldu \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Setja inn - Hlutur - Formúla\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id1276589				0	is	You see the Math input window and the Elements window. If you don't see the Elements window, you can enable it in the View menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id3283791				0	is	In the upper part of the Elements window, click the \<emph\>Operators\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id9734794				0	is	In the lower part of the Elements window, click the \<emph\>Sum\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id9641712				0	is	To enable lower and upper limits, click additionally the \<emph\>Upper and Lower Limits\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id3304239				0	is	In the input window, the first placeholder or marker is selected, and you can start to enter the lower limit: 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id8679158				0	is	k = 0				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id8471327				0	is	Press F4 to advance to the next marker, and enter the upper limit:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id4731894				0	is	n				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id759300				0	is	Press F4 to advance to the next marker, and enter the summand:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id651875				0	is	s^k				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id6756187				0	is	Now the formula is complete. Click into your text document outside the formula to leave the formula editor.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id9406414				0	is	In the same way, you can enter an Integral formula with limits. When you click an icon from the Elements window, the assigned text command is inserted in the input window. If you know the text commands, you can enter the commands directly in the input window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id5866267				0	is	Veldu \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Setja inn - Hlutur - Formúla\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id1965697				0	is	Click in the input window and enter the following line:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id9004486				0	is	int from{a} to{b} f(x)`dx				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id4651020				0	is	A small gap exists between f(x) and dx, which you can also enter using the Elements window: click the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> icon, then the \<emph\>Small Gap\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id3877071				0	is	If you don't like the font of the letters f and x, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Fonts\</item\> and select other fonts. Click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button to use the new fonts as default from now on.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id3021332				0	is	If you need the formula within a line of text, the limits increase the line height. You can choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Text Mode\</item\> to place the limits besides the Sum or Integral symbol, which reduces the line height.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id260322				0	is	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090909.xhp\"\>Example of Integral and Sum ranges\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
