helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150298				0	is	You can control $[officename] Math without a mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150343				0	is	Inserting a Formula Directly				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154659				0	is	If you want to insert a formula into a text document, and you already know the correct writing, you can proceed as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	is	Write the formula into your text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915				0	is	Select the formula				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	is	Choose the command \<emph\>Insert - Object - Formula\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154767				0	is	Inserting a Formula using a Window				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149875				0	is	If you want to use the $[officename] Math interface to edit a formula, choose the command \<emph\>Insert - Object - Formula\</emph\> without any text selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	is	The cursor waits in the Commands window and you can type the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537				0	is	You can compose formulas using the Elements window. Open it with the menu \<emph\>View - Elements\</emph\> if it is not already open.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155625				0	is	If the Elements window is open, use F6 to switch from the Commands window to the Elements window and back.				20181231 09:50:43
