helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152963				0	is	Sérsniðnar leturgerðir				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154566				0	is	In this section of the \<emph\>Fonts\</emph\> dialog you can define fonts, with which you can format other text components in the formula. The three basic fonts \<emph\>Serif, Sans\</emph\> and \<emph\>Fixed\</emph\> are available. You can add any other font to each standard installed basic font. Every font installed on your system is available for you to use. Select the \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> button to expand the selection offered in the list box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151315	17			0	is	These custom fonts are used if you set a different font with the FONT command in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153670				0	is	Serif				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151108				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:5\"\>You can specify the font to be used for the \<emph\>font serif\</emph\> format.\</ahelp\> Serifs are the small "guides" that can be seen, for example, at the bottom of a capital A when the Times serif font is used. Using serifs is quite helpful since it guides a reader's eye in a straight line and can speed up reading.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150836				0	is	Sans				20181231 09:50:43
