helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153505				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_NEGX\"\>Inserts a \<emph\>Boolean NOT\</emph\> with one placeholder.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>neg<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10383				0	is	\<image id=\"img_id3147116\" src=\"starmath/res/un21214.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147116\"\>Táknmynd\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149847				0	is	Boole gildið OG				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147599				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XANDY\"\>Inserts a \<emph\>Boolean AND\</emph\> with two placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\><?>and<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_idN103C3				0	is	\<image id=\"img_id3148440\" src=\"starmath/res/un21215.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148440\"\>Táknmynd\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151086				0	is	Boole gildið EÐA				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154076				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XORY\"\>Inserts a \<emph\>Boolean OR\</emph\> with two placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\><?>or<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10403				0	is	\<image id=\"img_id3150173\" src=\"starmath/res/un21221.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150173\"\>Táknmynd\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151129				0	is	Setja saman				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156102	39			0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XCIRCY\"\>Inserts a \<emph\>concatenation sign\</emph\> with two placeholders. \</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>circ\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150464				0	is	You can also insert user-defined unary operators by typing \<emph\>uoper\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window, followed by the syntax for the character. This function is useful for incorporating special characters into a formula. For example, the command \<emph\>uoper %theta x\</emph\> produces a small Greek letter theta (a component of the \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\> character set). You can also insert characters not in the $[officename] character set by choosing \<emph\>Tools - Catalog - Edit\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154725				0	is	 You can also insert user-defined binary commands by typing \<emph\>boper\</emph\> into the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window. For example, the command \<emph\>y boper %theta x\</emph\> produces the small Greek letter theta preceded by a \<emph\>y\</emph\> and followed by an \<emph\>x\</emph\>. You can also insert characters not in the $[officename] character set by choosing \<emph\>Tools - Catalog - Edit\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150906				0	is	By typing \<emph\><?>oplus<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window, you insert a \<emph\>circled plus operator\</emph\> in your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151197				0	is	Type \<emph\><?>ominus<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to insert a \<emph\>circled minus operator\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155082				0	is	Type \<emph\><?>odot<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to insert a \<emph\>circled dot operator\</emph\> in the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154331				0	is	Type \<emph\><?>odivide<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to insert a \<emph\>circled division operator\</emph\> in the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150089				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XWIDESLASHY\"\>Type \<emph\>a wideslash b\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to produce two characters with a slash (from lower left to upper right) between them.\</ahelp\> The characters are set such that everything to the left of the slash is up, and everything to the right is down. This command is also available in the context menu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150024				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XWIDEBSLASHY\"\>Type \<emph\>a widebslash b\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to produce two characters with a slash (from upper left to lower right) between them.\</ahelp\> The characters are set such that everything to the left of the slash is down, and everything to the right is up. This command is also available in the context menu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149376				0	is	Type \<emph\>sub\</emph\> or \<emph\>sup\</emph\> in the Commands window to add indexes and powers to the characters in your formula; for example, a sub 2.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155383				0	is	If you want to use a colon ':' as division sign, choose \<emph\>Tools - Catalog\</emph\> or click the \<emph\>Catalog\</emph\> icon on the Tools bar. Click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> button in the dialog that appears, then select the \<emph\>Special\</emph\> symbol set. Enter a meaningful name next to \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\>, for example, "divide" and then click the colon in the set of symbols. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> and then \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the \<emph\>Symbols\</emph\> dialog,too. Now you can use the new symbol, in this case the colon, by entering its name in the Commands window, for example, \<emph\>a %divide b = c\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147398				0	is	When entering information manually in the Commands window, please note that a number of operators require spaces between the elements for the correct structure. This is especially true if you are using values instead of placeholders in your operators, for example, to construct a division 4 div 3 or a div b.				20181231 09:50:43
