helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_bubble.xhp	0	help	hd_id1970722				0	is	\<variable id=\"type_bubble\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_bubble.xhp\"\>Chart Type Bubble\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_bubble.xhp	0	help	par_id40589				0	is	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_bubble.xhp	0	help	hd_id0526200904491284				0	is	Blaðra				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_bubble.xhp	0	help	par_id0526200904491222				0	is	A bubble chart shows the relations of three variables. Two variables are used for the position on the X-axis and Y-axis, while the third variable is shown as the relative size of each bubble.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_bubble.xhp	0	help	par_id0526200906040162				0	is	The data series dialog for a bubble chart has an entry to define the data range for the Bubble Sizes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Chart Wizard - Data Range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	bm_id2429578				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>data ranges in charts\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	hd_id8313852				0	is	\<variable id=\"wiz_data_range\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_range.xhp\"\>Línuritahjálp - Gagnabil\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id8829309				0	is	On this page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can select one single source of data range. This range may consist of more than one rectangular range of cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id6401867				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Data Ranges dialog where you can edit Data Range and Data Series.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id2025818				0	is	Use the Chart Wizard - Data Series page if you need more control over the data ranges.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id8466139				0	is	This dialog is only available for charts based on a Calc or Writer table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	hd_id1877193				0	is	To specify a data range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5924863				0	is	Select the data range. Do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id4357432				0	is	Enter the data range in the text box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5626392				0	is	In Calc, an example data range would be "$Sheet1.$B$3:$B$14". Note that a data range may consist of more than one region in a spreadsheet, e.g. "$Sheet1.A1:A5;$Sheet1.D1:D5" is also a valid data range. In Writer, an example data range would be "Table1.A1:E4".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id1363872				0	is	In Calc, click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog, then drag over a cell area to select the data range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id6823938				0	is	If you want a data range of multiple cell areas that are not next to each other, enter the first range, then manually add a semicolon at the end of the text box, then enter the other ranges. Use a semicolon as delimiter between ranges.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id1434369				0	is	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id7524033				0	is	Check whether the data range has labels in the first row or in the first column or both.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5256508				0	is	In the preview you can see how the final chart will look.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id379650				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the data range that you want to include in your chart. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id953703				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Data series get their data from consecutive rows in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data series will contain x-values for all series. All other data series are used as y-values, one for each series.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id4496597				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Data series get their data from consecutive columns in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data column will contain x-values for all series. All other data columns are used as y-values, one for each series.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id2898953				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For data series in columns: The first row in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first row in the range is used as categories. The remaining rows comprise the data series. If this check box is not selected, all rows are data series.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id7546311				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For data series in columns: The first column in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first column in the range is used as categories. The remaining columns comprise the data columns. If this check box is not selected, all columns are data columns.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Stilling				20181231 09:50:43
