helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	is	\<variable id=\"statistik\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Use the \<emph\>Y Error Bars\</emph\> dialog to display error bars for 2D charts.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3401287				0	is	An error bar is an indicator line that spans over a range from y - NegativeErrorValue to y + PositiveErrorValue. In this term, y is the value of the data point. When "standard deviation" is selected, y is the mean value of the data series. NegativeErrorValue and PositiveErrorValue are the amounts calculated by the error bar function or given explicitly.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	is	The \<emph\>Insert - Y Error Bars\</emph\> menu command is only available for 2D charts.				20181231 09:50:43
