helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150542				0	is	\<variable id=\"html_doc\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/html_doc.xhp\" name=\"Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\"\>Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154124				0	is	Saving Sheets in HTML				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	is	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc saves all the sheets of a Calc document together as an HTML document. At the beginning of the HTML document, a heading and a list of hyperlinks are automatically added which lead to the individual sheets within the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	is	Numbers are shown as written. In addition, in the <SDVAL> HTML tag, the exact internal number value is written so that after opening the HTML document with \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> you know you have the exact values.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	is	To save the current Calc document as HTML, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	is	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> list box, in the area with the other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc filters, choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	is	Enter a \<emph\>File name\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149379				0	is	Opening Sheets in HTML				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	is	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> offers various filters for opening HTML files, which you can select under \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Files of type\</emph\> list box:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	is	Choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446				0	is	All \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc options are now available to you. However, not all options that \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc offers for editing can be saved in HTML format.				20181231 09:50:43
