helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id9520249				0	is	You can define a background color or use a graphic as a background for cell ranges in $[officename] Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144760				0	is	Applying a Background Color to a $[officename] Calc Spreadsheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429				0	is	Veldu reitina.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	is	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> (or \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> from the context menu).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3152938				0	is	On the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page, select the background color.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146974				0	is	Graphics in the Background of Cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155414				0	is	Veldu \<emph\>Setja inn - Mynd - Mynd úr skrá\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	is	Select the graphic and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153575				0	is	The graphic is inserted anchored to the current cell. You can move and scale the graphic as you want. In your context menu you can use the \<emph\>Arrange - To Background\</emph\> command to place this in the background. To select a graphic that has been placed in the background, use the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Navigator\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id51576				0	is	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/background.xhp\"\>Watermarks\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156180				0	is	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030600.xhp\" name=\"Background tab page\"\>\<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id7601245				0	is	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_table.xhp\"\>Formatting Spreadsheets\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Formatting Spreadsheets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154125				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; formatting options for selected cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currencies;formats\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154125				0	is	\<variable id=\"format_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_table.xhp\" name=\"Designing Spreadsheets\"\>Formatting Spreadsheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153912	13			0	is	Formatting Text in a Spreadsheet 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3144772				0	is	Veldu textann sem á að sníða.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155268	15			0	is	Choose the desired text attributes from the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>Bar. You can also choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog will appear in which you can choose various text attributes on the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149899				0	is	Formatting Numbers in a Spreadsheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3159226				0	is	Select the cells containing the numbers you want to format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3150046	18			0	is	To format numbers in the default currency format or as percentages, use the icons on the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>Bar. For other formats, choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. You can choose from the preset formats or define your own on the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153483				0	is	Formatting Borders and Backgrounds for Cells and Pages				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154733				0	is	You can assign a format to any group of cells by first selecting the cells (for multiple selection, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key when clicking), and then activating the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cell\</item\>. In this dialog, you can select attributes such as shadows and backgrounds.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116				0	is	To apply formatting attributes to an entire sheet, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>. You can define headers and footers, for example, to appear on each printed page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145389				0	is	An image that you have loaded with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Background\</item\> is only visible in print or in the page preview. To display a background image on screen as well, insert the graphic image by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Picture - From File\</item\> and arrange the image behind the cells by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Arrange - To Background\</item\>. Use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> to select the background image.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id2837916				0	is	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\"\>Number Formatting Options\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id2614215				0	is	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/background.xhp\"\>Backgrounds for Cells\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	19xx/20xx ár				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150439				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>years; 2-digits\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dates; 19xx/20xx\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150439				0	is	\<variable id=\"year2000\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/year2000.xhp\" name=\"19xx/20xx ár\"\>19xx/20xx ár\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116				0	is	The year in a date entry is often entered as two digits. Internally, the year is managed by $[officename] as four digits, so that in the calculation of the difference from 1/1/99 to 1/1/01, the result will correctly be two years.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	is	Under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - General\</emph\> you can define the century that is used when you enter a year with only two digits. The default is 1930 to 2029.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	is	This means that if you enter a date of 1/1/30 or higher, it will be treated internally as 1/1/1930 or higher. All lower two-digit years apply to the 20xx century. So, for example, 1/1/20 is converted into 1/1/2020.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>HTML WebQuery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ranges; inserting in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>external data; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; inserting external data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>web pages; importing data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>WebQuery filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; external data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources; external data\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	is	\<variable id=\"webquery\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/webquery.xhp\" name=\"Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)\"\>Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	is	With the help of the \<emph\>Web Page Query ($[officename] Calc)\</emph\> import filter, you can insert tables from HTML documents in a Calc spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	is	You can use the same method to insert ranges defined by name from a Calc or Microsoft Excel spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	is	The following insert methods are available:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146976				0	is	Inserting by Dialog				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	is	Set the cell cursor at the cell where the new content will be inserted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	is	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Link to External Data\</emph\>. This opens the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\"\>External Data\</link\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	is	Enter the URL of the HTML document or the name of the spreadsheet. Press Enter when finished. Click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to open a file selection dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	is	In the large list box of the dialog, select the named ranges or tables you want to insert.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	is	You can also specify that the ranges or tables are updated every n seconds.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	is	The import filter can create names for cell ranges on the fly. As much formatting as possible is retained, while the filter intentionally does not load any images.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149021				0	is	Inserting by Navigator				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	is	Open two documents: the $[officename] Calc spreadsheet in which the external data is to be inserted (target document) and the document from which the external data derives (source document).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3150205				0	is	In the target document open the Navigator.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	is	In the lower combo box of the Navigator select the source document. The Navigator now shows the range names and database ranges or the tables contained in the source document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3148842	20			0	is	In the Navigator select the \<emph\>Insert as link\</emph\> drag mode \<image id=\"img_id3152985\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20238.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152985\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3157978				0	is	Drag the desired external data from the Navigator into the target document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	is	If you have loaded an HTML document with the \<emph\>Web Page Query\</emph\> filter as the source document, you will find the tables in the Navigator, named continuously from "HTML_table1" onwards, and also two range names that have been created:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3152873				0	is	\<item type=\"literal\"\>HTML_all\</item\> - designates the entire document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149897				0	is	\<item type=\"literal\"\>HTML_tables\</item\> - designates all HTML tables in the document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149126				0	is	Editing the external data				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3159228				0	is	Open \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\>. Here you can edit the link to the external data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154650				0	is	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"External data dialog\"\>External data dialog\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
