helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154684				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>tables; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title rows; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>freezing rows or columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scrolling prevention in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>windows; splitting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; splitting windows\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154684				0	is	\<variable id=\"line_fix\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/line_fix.xhp\" name=\"Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\"\>Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	is	If you have long rows or columns of data that extend beyond the viewable area of the sheet, you can freeze some rows or columns, which allows you to see the frozen columns or rows as you scroll through the rest of the data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	is	Select the row below, or the column to the right of the row or column that you want to be in the frozen region. All rows above, or all columns to the left of the selection are frozen.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	is	To freeze both horizontally and vertically, select the \<emph\>cell\</emph\> that is below the row and to the right of the column that you want to freeze.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	is	Veldu \<emph\>Gluggi - Frysta\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073	5			0	is	To deactivate, choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze \</emph\>again.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	is	If the area defined is to be scrollable, apply the \<emph\>Window - Split\</emph\> command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	is	If you want to print a certain row on all pages of a document, choose \<emph\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147004				0	is	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07090000.xhp\" name=\"Gluggi - Frysta\"\>Gluggi - Frysta\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	is	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07080000.xhp\" name=\"Gluggi - Kljúfa\"\>Gluggi - Kljúfa\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	is	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Print ranges - Edit\"\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Cells in Currency Format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156329				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>currency formats; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>international currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; currency formats in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currencies; default currencies\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156329				0	is	\<variable id=\"currency_format\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/currency_format.xhp\" name=\"Cells in Currency Format\"\>Cells in Currency Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	is	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can give numbers any currency format. When you click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Currency\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3150791\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_currencyfield.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150791\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> bar to format a number, the cell is given the default currency format set under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	is	Exchanging of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc documents can lead to misunderstandings, if your \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc document is loaded by a user who uses a different default currency format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	is	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can define that a number that you have formatted as "1,234.50 €", still remains in euros in another country and does not become dollars.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075				0	is	You can change the currency format in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format Cells\</item\> dialog (choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</item\> tab) by two country settings. In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Language\</item\> combo box select the basic setting for decimal and thousands separators. In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list box you can select the currency symbol and its position.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	is	For example, if the language is set to "Default" and you are using a german locale setting, the currency format will be "1.234,00 €". A point is used before the thousand digits and a comma before the decimal places. If you now select the subordinate currency format "$ English (US)" from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list box , you will get the following format: "$ 1.234,00". As you can see, the separators have remained the same. Only the currency symbol has been changed and converted, but the underlying format of the notation remains the same as in the locale setting.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	is	If, under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Language\</item\>, you convert the cells to "English (US)", the English-language locale setting is also transferred and the default currency format is now "$ 1,234.00".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	is	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Sníða - Reitir - Tölustafir\"\>Sníða - Reitir - Tölustafir\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Entering Matrix Formulas				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153969				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>matrices; entering matrix formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; matrix formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;matrix formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153969				0	is	\<variable id=\"matrixformula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/matrixformula.xhp\" name=\"Entering Matrix Formulas\"\>Entering Matrix Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	is	The following is an example of how you can enter a matrix formula, without going into the details of matrix functions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	is	Assume you have entered 10 numbers in Columns A and B (A1:A10 and B1:B10), and would like to calculate the sum of each row in Column C.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321				0	is	Using the mouse, select the range C1:C10, in which the results are to be displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	is	Press F2, or click in the input line of the Formula bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	is	Enter an equal sign (=).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	is	Select the range A1:A10, which contains the first values for the sum formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3144767				0	is	Press the (+) key from the numerical keypad.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	is	Select the numbers in the second column in cells B1:B10.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150716				0	is	End the input with the matrix key combination: Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	is	The matrix area is automatically protected against modifications, such as deleting rows or columns. It is, however, possible to edit any formatting, such as the cell background.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Formatting Numbers as Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>numbers;entering as text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text formats; for numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; numbers as text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell formats; text/numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbers as text\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	is	\<variable id=\"text_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/text_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Numbers as Text\"\>Formatting Numbers as Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	is	You can format numbers as text in $[officename] Calc. Open the context menu of a cell or range of cells and choose \<emph\>Format Cells - Numbers\</emph\>, then select "Text" from the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> list. Any numbers subsequently entered into the formatted range are interpreted as text. The display of these "numbers" is left-justified, just as with other text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	is	If you have already entered normal numbers in cells and have afterwards changed the format of the cells to "Text", the numbers will remain normal numbers. They will not be converted. Only numbers entered afterwards, or numbers which are then edited, will become text numbers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3144765				0	is	If you decide to enter a number directly as text, enter an apostrophe (') first. For example, for years in column headings, you can enter '1999, '2000 and '2001. The apostrophe is not visible in the cell, it only indicates that the entry is to be recognized as a text. This is useful if, for example, you enter a telephone number or postal code that begins with a zero (0), because a zero (0) at the start of a sequence of digits is removed in normal number formats.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	is	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Sníða - Reitir - Tölustafir\"\>Sníða - Reitir - Tölustafir\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Applying Goal Seek				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>goal seeking;example\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>equations in goal seek\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;variables in equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variables;calculating equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples;goal seek\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	is	\<variable id=\"goalseek\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/goalseek.xhp\" name=\"Applying Goal Seek\"\>Applying Goal Seek\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	is	With the help of Goal Seek you can calculate a value that, as part of a formula, leads to the result you specify for the formula. You thus define the formula with several fixed values and one variable value and the result of the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153966				0	is	Goal Seek Example				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150871				0	is	To calculate annual interest (I), create a table with the values for the capital (C), number of years (n), and interest rate (i). The formula is:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	is	I = C * n* i				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	is	Let us assume that the interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> of 7.5% and the number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\> (1) will remain constant. However, you want to know how much the investment capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would have to be modified in order to attain a particular return \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\>. For this example, calculate how much capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would be required if you want an annual return of $15,000.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	is	Enter each of the values for Capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> (an arbitrary value like \<item type=\"literal\"\>$100,000\</item\>), number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n \</item\>(\<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\>), and interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> (\<item type=\"literal\"\>7.5%\</item\>) in one cell each. Enter the formula to calculate the interest \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\> in another cell. Instead of \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\>, and \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/relativ_absolut_ref.xhp\"\>reference to the cell\</link\> with the corresponding value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	is	Place the cursor in the cell containing the interest \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\>, and choose \<emph\>Tools - Goal Seek\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Goal Seek\</emph\> dialog appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	is	The correct cell is already entered in the field \<emph\>Formula Cell\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	is	Place the cursor in the field \<emph\>Variable Cell\</emph\>. In the sheet, click in the cell that contains the value to be changed, in this example it is the cell with the capital value \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150369				0	is	Enter the expected result of the formula in the \<emph\>Target Value\</emph\> text box. In this example, the value is 15,000. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3146978				0	is	A dialog appears informing you that the Goal Seek was successful. Click \<emph\>Yes\</emph\> to enter the result in the cell with the variable value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3149409				0	is	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Markaleit\"\>Markaleit\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
