helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150767				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; sorting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sorting; database ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>data;sorting in databases\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150767				0	is	\<variable id=\"database_sort\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_sort.xhp\" name=\"Sorting Database Ranges\"\>Sorting Data\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3145751				0	is	Click in a database range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id121020081121549				0	is	If you select a range of cells, only these cells will get sorted. If you just click one cell without selecting, then the whole database range will get sorted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN10635				0	is	Veldu \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Gögn - Raða\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id121020081121547				0	is	The range of cells that will get sorted is shown in inverted colors.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	is	Select the sort options that you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063D				0	is	Smelltu á \<emph\>Í lagi\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id1846980				0	is	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Defining_a_Data_Range\"\>Wiki page about defining a data range\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Referencing a Cell in Another Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147436				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>sheet references\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references; to cells in other sheets/documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; operating in another document\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents;references\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436				0	is	\<variable id=\"cellreferences\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences.xhp\" name=\"Referencing Other Sheets\"\>Referencing Other Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9663075				0	is	In a sheet cell you can show a reference to a cell in another sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id1879329				0	is	In the same way, a reference can also be made to a cell from another document provided that this document has already been saved as a file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id7122409				0	is	To Reference a Cell in the Same Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id2078005				0	is	Open a new, empty spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id4943693				0	is	By way of example, enter the following formula in cell A1 of Sheet1:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9064302				0	is	               \<item type=\"literal\"\>=Sheet2.A1\</item\>            				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7609790				0	is	Click the \<emph\>Sheet 2\</emph\> tab at the bottom of the spreadsheet. Set the cursor in cell A1 there and enter text or a number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id809961				0	is	If you switch back to Sheet1, you will see the same content in cell A1 there. If the contents of Sheet2.A1 change, then the contents of Sheet1.A1 also change.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id9209570				0	is	To Reference a Cell in Another Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5949278				0	is	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>, to load an existing spreadsheet document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8001953				0	is	Choose \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, to open a new spreadsheet document. Set the cursor in the cell where you want to insert the external data and enter an equals sign to indicate that you want to begin a formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8571123				0	is	Now switch to the document you have just loaded. Click the cell with the data that you want to insert in the new document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8261665				0	is	Switch back to the new spreadsheet. In the input line you will now see how $[officename] Calc has added the reference to the formula for you. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5888241				0	is	The reference to a cell of another document contains the name of the other document in single inverted commas, then a hash #, then the name of the sheet of the other document, followed by a point and the name of the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7697683				0	is	Confirm the formula by clicking the green check mark.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7099826				0	is	If you drag the box in the lower right corner of the active cell to select a range of cells, $[officename] automatically inserts the corresponding references in the adjacent cells. As a result, the sheet name is preceded with a "$" sign to designate it as an absolute reference.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id674459				0	is	If you examine the name of the other document in this formula, you will notice that it is written as a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\>. This means that you can also enter a URL from the Internet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Addresses and References, Absolute and Relative				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>addressing; relative and absolute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; absolute/relative\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>absolute addresses in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative addresses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>absolute references in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; to cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; references\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	is	\<variable id=\"relativ_absolut_ref\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/relativ_absolut_ref.xhp\" name=\"Addresses and References, Absolute and Relative\"\>Addresses and References, Absolute and Relative\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163712				0	is	Relative Addressing				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	is	The cell in column A, row 1 is addressed as A1. You can address a range of adjacent cells by first entering the coordinates of the upper left cell of the area, then a colon followed by the coordinates of the lower right cell. For example, the square formed by the first four cells in the upper left corner is addressed as A1:B2.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730				0	is	By addressing an area in this way, you are making a relative reference to A1:B2. Relative here means that the reference to this area will be adjusted automatically when you copy the formulas.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149377				0	is	Absolute Addressing				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3154943				0	is	Absolute references are the opposite of relative addressing. A dollar sign is placed before each letter and number in an absolute reference, for example, $A$1:$B$2.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	is	$[officename] can convert the current reference, in which the cursor is positioned in the input line, from relative to absolute and vice versa by pressing Shift +F4. If you start with a relative address such as A1, the first time you press this key combination, both row and column are set to absolute references ($A$1). The second time, only the row (A$1), and the third time, only the column ($A1). If you press the key combination once more, both column and row references are switched back to relative (A1)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	is	$[officename] Calc shows the references to a formula. If, for example you click the formula =SUM(A1:C5;D15:D24) in a cell, the two referenced areas in the sheet will be highlighted in color. For example, the formula component "A1:C5" may be in blue and the cell range in question bordered in the same shade of blue. The next formula component "D15:D24" can be marked in red in the same way.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154704				0	is	When to Use Relative and Absolute References				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147346				0	is	What distinguishes a relative reference? Assume you want to calculate in cell E1 the sum of the cells in range A1:B2. The formula to enter into E1 would be: =SUM(A1:B2). If you later decide to insert a new column in front of column A, the elements you want to add would then be in B1:C2 and the formula would be in F1, not in E1. After inserting the new column, you would therefore have to check and correct all formulas in the sheet, and possibly in other sheets.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	is	Fortunately, $[officename] does this work for you. After having inserted a new column A, the formula =SUM(A1:B2) will be automatically updated to =SUM(B1:C2). Row numbers will also be automatically adjusted when a new row 1 is inserted. Absolute and relative references are always adjusted in $[officename] Calc whenever the referenced area is moved. But be careful if you are copying a formula since in that case only the relative references will be adjusted, not the absolute references.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3145791				0	is	Absolute references are used when a calculation refers to one specific cell in your sheet. If a formula that refers to exactly this cell is copied relatively to a cell below the original cell, the reference will also be moved down if you did not define the cell coordinates as absolute.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005				0	is	Aside from when new rows and columns are inserted, references can also change when an existing formula referring to particular cells is copied to another area of the sheet. Assume you entered the formula =SUM(A1:A9) in row 10. If you want to calculate the sum for the adjacent column to the right, simply copy this formula to the cell to the right. The copy of the formula in column B will be automatically adjusted to =SUM(B1:B9).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Finding and Replacing in Calc				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id3769341				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding;formulas/values/text/objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing; cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;multiple cell texts\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149204				0	is	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Calc\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9363689				0	is	In spreadsheet documents you can find words, formulas, and styles. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all matching cells at once, then apply another format or replace the cell content by other content.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3610644				0	is	The Find & Replace dialog				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	is	Cells can contain text or numbers that were entered directly as in a text document. But cells can also contain text or numbers as the result of a calculation. For example, if a cell contains the formula =1+2 it displays the result 3. You must decide whether to search for the 1 respective 2, or to search the 3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id2423780				0	is	To find formulas or values				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	is	You can specify in the Find & Replace dialog either to find the parts of a formula or the results of a calculation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6394238				0	is	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7214270				0	is	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2186346				0	is	Select "Formulas" or "Values" in the \<emph\>Search in\</emph\> list box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	is	With "Formulas" you will find all parts of the formulas. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id393993				0	is	With "Values" you will find the results of the calculations. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	is	Cell contents can be formatted in different ways. For example, a number can be formatted as a currency, to be displayed with a currency symbol. You see the currency symbol in the cell, but you cannot search for it.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id7359233				0	is	Finding text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6549272				0	is	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6529740				0	is	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9121982				0	is	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3808404				0	is	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Calc will select the next cell that contains your text. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found cell. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2394482				0	is	If you closed the dialog, you can press a key combination (\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+F) to find the next cell without opening the dialog. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id631733				0	is	By default, Calc searches the current sheet. Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\>, then enable \<emph\>Search in all sheets\</emph\> to search through all sheets of the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	is	When you click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>, Calc selects all cells that contain your entry. Now you can for example set all found cells to bold, or apply a Cell Style to all at once.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8531449				0	is	The Navigator				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	is	Choose \<emph\>View - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	is	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	is	Use the Navigator for inserting objects and links within the same document or from other open documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Calculating in Spreadsheets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; calculating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; calculating\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791				0	is	\<variable id=\"calculate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calculate.xhp\" name=\"Calculating in Spreadsheets\"\>Calculating in Spreadsheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	is	The following is an example of a calculation in $[officename] Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	is	Click in a cell, and type a number				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN10656				0	is	Smelltu á Enter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065D				0	is	The cursor moves down to the next cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	is	Enter another number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066F				0	is	Press the Tab key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN10676				0	is	The cursor moves to the right into the next cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	is	Type in a formula, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=A3 * A4 / 100.\</item\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068B				0	is	 Smelltu á Enter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	is	The result of the formula appears in the cell. If you want, you can edit the formula in the input line of the Formula bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155378				0	is	When you edit a formula, the new result is calculated automatically.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Displaying Formulas or Values				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153195				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>formulas; displaying in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values; displaying in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; displaying formulas/values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>results display vs. formulas display\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>displaying; formulas instead of results\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153195				0	is	\<variable id=\"formula_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_value.xhp\" name=\"Displaying Formulas or Values\"\>Displaying Formulas or Values\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	is	If you want to display the formulas in the cells, for example in the form =SUM(A1:B5), proceed as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116				0	is	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	is	In the \<emph\>Display\</emph\> area mark the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> box. Click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	is	If you want to view the calculation results instead of the formula, do not mark the Formulas box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	is	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Defining Number of Pages for Printing				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153194				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheet counts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing sheet counts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page breaks; spreadsheet preview\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>previews;page breaks for printing\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153194				0	is	\<variable id=\"print_exact\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_exact.xhp\" name=\"Defining Number of Pages for Printing\"\>Defining Number of Pages for Printing\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	is	If a sheet is too large for a single printed page, $[officename] Calc will print the current sheet evenly divided over several pages. Since the automatic page break does not always take place in the optimal position, you can define the page distribution yourself.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155				0	is	Go to the sheet to be printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012				0	is	Veldu \<emph\>Skoða - Forskoðun síðuskila\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	is	You will see the automatic distribution of the sheet across the print pages. The automatically created print ranges are indicated by dark blue lines, and the user-defined ones by light blue lines. The page breaks (line breaks and column breaks) are marked as black lines.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	is	You can move the blue lines with the mouse. You will find further options in the Context menu, including adding an additional print range, removing the scaling and inserting additional manual line and column breaks.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	is	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"Skoða - Forskoðun síðuskila\"\>Skoða - Forskoðun síðuskila\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Entering a Number with Leading Zeros				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147560				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>zero values; entering leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>integers with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; changing text/number formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; changing text/number\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells; changing to numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>converting;text with leading zeros, into numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147560				0	is	\<variable id=\"integer_leading_zero\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/integer_leading_zero.xhp\" name=\"Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\"\>Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194				0	is	There are various ways to enter integers starting with a zero:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	is	Enter the number as text. The easiest way is to enter the number starting with an apostrophe (for example, \<item type=\"input\"\>'0987\</item\>). The apostrophe will not appear in the cell, and the number will be formatted as text. Because it is in text format, however, you cannot calculate with this number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	is	Format a cell with a number format such as \<item type=\"input\"\>\\0000\</item\>. This format can be assigned in the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> field under the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\> tab, and defines the cell display as "always put a zero first and then the integer, having at least three places, and filled with zeros at the left if less than three digits".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	is	If you want to apply a numerical format to a column of numbers in text format (for example, text "000123" becomes number "123"), do the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	is	Select the column in which the digits are found in text format. Set the cell format in that column as "Number".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	60			0	is	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>               				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510	61			0	is	In the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>^[0-9]\</item\>               				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068	62			0	is	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>&\</item\>               				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018	63			0	is	Check \<emph\>Regular expressions\</emph\>               				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	64			0	is	\<emph\>Eingöngu núverandi val\</emph\>Haka               				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146916	65			0	is	\<emph\>Breyta öllu\</emph\>Smella               				20181231 09:50:43
