helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Shortcut Keys (%PRODUCTNAME Calc Accessibility)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145120				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; %PRODUCTNAME Calc shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>shortcut keys;%PRODUCTNAME Calc accessibility\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145120				0	is	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcut Keys (%PRODUCTNAME Calc Accessibility)\"\>Shortcut Keys (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	is	Refer also to the lists of shortcut keys for \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> in general.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153360				0	is	Cell Selection Mode				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	is	\<image id=\"img_id3150439\" src=\"formula/res/refinp1.png\" width=\"0.1327inch\" height=\"0.1327inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150439\"\>Táknmynd\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	is	In a text box that has a button to minimize the dialog, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\> to enter the cell selection mode. Select any number of cells, then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\> again to show the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	is	In the cell selection mode, you can use the common navigation keys to select cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148646				0	is	Controlling the Outline				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	is	You can use the keyboard in \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"Outline\"\>Outline\</link\>:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	is	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F6\</item\> until the vertical or horizontal outline window has the focus.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	is	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons from top to bottom or from left to right.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	is	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons in the opposite direction.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149403				0	is	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+1 to Command+8\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+1 to Ctrl+8\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - show all levels up to the specified number; hide all higher levels.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	is	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>+\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>-\</item\> to show or hide the focused outline group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446				0	is	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> to activate the focused button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	is	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Up\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Down\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Left\</item\>, or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> arrow to cycle through all buttons in the current level.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147343				0	is	Selecting a Drawing Object or a Graphic				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AA				0	is	Choose View - Toolbars - Drawing to open the Drawing toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	is	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> until the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar is selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345				0	is	If the selection tool is active, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter. This selects the first drawing object or graphic in the sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159240				0	is	Með \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Val\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 setur þú fókus á skjalið.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155379				0	is	Now you can use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> to select the next drawing object or graphic and \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> to select the previous one.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	References to Other Sheets and Referencing URLs				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150441				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; in sheet cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; URL in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; Internet references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL; in Calc\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150441				0	is	\<variable id=\"cellreferences_url\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences_url.xhp\" name=\"Referencing URLs\"\>Referencing URLs\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id1955626				0	is	For example, if you found an Internet page containing current stock exchange information in spreadsheet cells, you can load this page in $[officename] Calc by using the following procedure:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993				0	is	In a $[officename] Calc document, position the cursor in the cell into which you want to insert the external data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	is	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Link to External Data\</item\>. The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"External Data\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>External Data\</item\>\</link\> dialog appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152892				0	is	Enter the URL of the document or Web page in the dialog. The URL must be in the format: http://www.my-bank.com/table.html. The URL for local or local area network files is the path seen in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153068				0	is	$[officename] loads the Web page or file in the "background", that is, without displaying it. In the large list box of the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>External Data\</item\> dialog, you can see the name of all the sheets or named ranges you can choose from.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	is	Select one or more sheets or named ranges. You can also activate the automatic update function every "n" seconds and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3157979				0	is	The contents will be inserted as a link in the $[officename] Calc document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	is	Save your spreadsheet. When you open it again later, $[officename] Calc will update the linked cells following an inquiry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3159204				0	is	Under \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040900.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - General\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - General\</item\>\</link\> you can choose to have the update, when opened, automatically carried out either always, upon request or never. The update can be started manually in the dialog under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Links\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Highlighting Negative Numbers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147434				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; highlighting negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>highlighting;negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>colors;negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats;colors for negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434				0	is	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_minusvalue\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp\" name=\"Highlighting Negative Numbers\"\>Highlighting Negative Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	is	You can format cells with a number format that highlights negative numbers in red. Alternatively, you can define your own number format in which negative numbers are highlighted in other colors.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	is	Select the cells and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	is	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab, select a number format and mark \<emph\>Negative numbers red\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	is	The cell number format is defined in two parts. The format for positive numbers and zero is defined in front of the semicolon; after the semicolon the formula for negative numbers is defined. You can change the code (RED) under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format code\</item\>. For example, instead of RED, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>YELLOW\</item\>. If the new code appears in the list after clicking the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Add\</item\> icon, this is a valid entry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Selecting Themes for Sheets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>theme selection for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>layout;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell styles; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791	6			0	is	\<variable id=\"design\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/design.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Themes for Sheets\"\>Selecting Themes for Sheets\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	is	$[officename] Calc comes with a predefined set of formatting themes that you can apply to your spreadsheets.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	is	Það er ekki hægt að bæta þemum við og ekki hægt að breyta þeim. En það er hægt að laga til útlitið á skjalinu eftir að þemað hefur verið sett á.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	is	Before you format a sheet with a theme, you have to apply at least one custom cell style to the cells on the sheet. You can then change the cell formatting by selecting and applying a theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	is	To apply a custom cell style to a cell, you can open the Styles and Formatting window and, in its lower list box, set the Custom Styles view. A list of the existing custom defined cell styles will be displayed. Double click a name from the Styles and Formatting window to apply this style to the selected cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	is	Þema sett á töflu:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920	15			0	is	Click the \<emph\>Choose Themes\</emph\> icon in the \<emph\>Tools\</emph\> bar. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	is	The \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog appears. This dialog lists the available themes for the whole spreadsheet and the Styles and Formatting window lists the custom styles for specific cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114	9			0	is	In the \<emph\>Theme Selection \</emph\>dialog, select the theme that you want to apply to the spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090				0	is	Smelltu á Í lagi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150201				0	is	As soon as you select another theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog, some of the properties of the custom style will be applied to the current spreadsheet. The modifications will be immediately visible in your spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146979				0	is	\<link href=\"text/scalc/02/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Val á þema\"\>Val á þema\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Converting Text to Numbers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>formats; text as numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>time format conversion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date formats;conversion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>converting;text, into numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id0908200901265171				0	is	\<variable id=\"numbers_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/numbers_text.xhp\" name=\"Converting Text to Numbers\"\>Converting Text to Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265127				0	is	Calc converts text inside cells to the respective numeric values if an unambiguous conversion is possible. If no conversion is possible, Calc returns a #VALUE! error.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265196				0	is	Only integer numbers including exponent are converted, and ISO 8601 dates and times in their extended formats with separators. Anything else, like fractional numbers with decimal separators or dates other than ISO 8601, is not converted, as the text string would be locale dependent. Leading and trailing blanks are ignored.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265220				0	is	The following ISO 8601 formats are converted:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265288				0	is	CCYY-MM-DD				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265267				0	is	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265248				0	is	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265374				0	is	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss,s				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265327				0	is	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.s				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265399				0	is	kl:mi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265347				0	is	hh:mm:ss				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265349				0	is	hh:mm:ss,s				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265342				0	is	hh:mm:ss.s				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265491				0	is	The century code CC may not be omitted. Instead of the T date and time separator, exactly one space character may be used.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265467				0	is	If a date is given, it must be a valid Gregorian calendar date. In this case the optional time must be in the range 00:00 to 23:59:59.99999...				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265420				0	is	If only a time string is given, it may have an hours value of more than 24, while minutes and seconds can have a maximum value of 59.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265448				0	is	The conversion is done for single arguments only, as in =A1+A2, or ="1E2"+1. Cell range arguments are not affected, so SUM(A1:A2) differs from A1+A2 if at least one of the two cells contain a convertible string.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id090820090126540				0	is	Strings inside formulas are also converted, such as in ="1999-11-22"+42, which returns the date 42 days after November 22nd, 1999. Calculations involving localized dates as strings inside the formula return an error. For example, the localized date string "11/22/1999" or "22.11.1999" cannot be used for the automatic conversion.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id1005200903485368				0	is	Dæmi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id1005200903485359				0	is	In A1 enter the text \<item type=\"literal\"\>'1e2\</item\> (which is converted to the number 100 internally).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id1005200903485341				0	is	In A2 enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>=A1+1\</item\> (which correctly results in 101).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265544				0	is	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Sníða - Reitir - Tölustafir\"\>Sníða - Reitir - Tölustafir\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Calculating With Dates and Times				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146120				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>dates; in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>times; in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;date and time formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>current date and time values\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146120				0	is	\<variable id=\"calc_date\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_date.xhp\" name=\"Calculating With Dates and Times\"\>Calculating With Dates and Times\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3154320				0	is	In $[officename] Calc, you can perform calculations with current date and time values. As an example, to find out exactly how old you are in seconds or hours, follow the following steps:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3150750				0	is	In a spreadsheet, enter your birthday in cell A1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3145642	14			0	is	Enter the following formula in cell A3: \<item type=\"literal\"\>=NOW()-A1\</item\>            				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3149020				0	is	After pressing the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key you will see the result in date format. Since the result should show the difference between two dates as a number of days, you must format cell A3 as a number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	is	Place the cursor in cell A3, right-click to open a context menu and choose \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	is	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format Cells\</item\> dialog appears. On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbers\</item\> tab, the "Number" category will appear already highlighted. The format is set to "General", which causes the result of a calculation containing date entries to be displayed as a date. To display the result as a number, set the number format to "-1,234" and close the dialog with the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	is	The number of days between today's date and the specified date is displayed in cell A3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	is	Experiment with some additional formulas: in A4 enter =A3*24 to calculate the hours, in A5 enter =A4*60 for the minutes, and in A6 enter =A5*60 for seconds. Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key after each formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3149207				0	is	The time since your date of birth will be calculated and displayed in the various units. The values are calculated as of the exact moment when you entered the last formula and pressed the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key. This value is not automatically updated, although "Now" continuously changes. In the \<emph\>Tools\</emph\> menu, the menu item \<emph\>Cell Contents - AutoCalculate\</emph\> is normally active; however, automatic calculation does not apply to the function NOW. This ensures that your computer is not solely occupied with updating the sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Calculating Time Differences				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;time differences\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>time differences\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769				0	is	\<variable id=\"calc_timevalues\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_timevalues.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Time Differences\"\>Calculating Time Differences\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	par_id3149263				0	is	If you want to calculate time differences, for example, the time between 23:30 and 01:10 in the same night, use the following formula:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	par_id3159153				0	is	=(B2<A2)+B2-A2				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	par_id3152598				0	is	The later time is B2 and the earlier time is A2. The result of the example is 01:40 or 1 hour and 40 minutes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	par_id3145271				0	is	In the formula, an entire 24-hour day has a value of 1 and one hour has a value of 1/24. The logical value in parentheses is 0 or 1, corresponding to 0 or 24 hours. The result returned by the formula is automatically issued in time format due to the sequence of the operands.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Applying Sort Lists				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150870				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>filling;customized lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sort lists;applying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;sort lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>geometric lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arithmetic lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>series;sort lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists; user-defined\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>customized lists\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150870	3			0	is	\<variable id=\"sorted_list\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/sorted_list.xhp\" name=\"Applying Sort Lists\"\>Applying Sort Lists\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3159154				0	is	Sort lists allow you to type one piece of information in a cell, then drag it to fill in a consecutive list of items.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	is	For example, enter the text "Jan" or "January" in an empty cell. Select the cell and click the mouse on the lower right corner of the cell border. Then drag the selected cell a few cells to the right or downwards. When you release the mouse button, the highlighted cells will be filled with the names of the months.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id2367931				0	is	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>if you do not want to fill the cells with different values.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	is	The predefined series can be found under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</emph\>. You can also create your own lists of text strings tailored to your needs, such as a list of your company's branch offices. When you use the information in these lists later (for example, as headings), just enter the first name in the list and expand the entry by dragging it with your mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	is	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060400.xhp\" name=\"Röðun lista\"\>Röðun lista\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
