helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10953				0	is	Using the Page Break Preview to Edit Print Ranges				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093E				0	is	In the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, print ranges as well as page break regions are outlined by a blue border and contain a centered page number in gray. Nonprinting areas have a gray background.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	is	To define a new page break region, drag the border to a new location. When you define a new page break region, an automatic page break is replaced by a manual page break.				20181231 09:50:43
