helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Importing and Exporting Text Files				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153726				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>csv files;formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas; importing/exporting as csv files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>exporting;formulas as csv files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>importing;csv files with formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726				0	is	\<variable id=\"csv_formula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_formula.xhp\" name=\"Importing and Exporting Text Files\"\>Importing and Exporting CSV Text Files with Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149402				0	is	Comma separated values (CSV) files are text files that contain the cell contents of a single sheet. Commas, semicolons, or other characters can be used as the field delimiters between the cells. Text strings are put in quotation marks, numbers are written without quotation marks.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715				0	is	To Import a CSV File				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153709				0	is	Veldu \<emph\>Skrá - Opna\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155445				0	is	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> field, select the format "Text CSV". Select the file and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When a file has the .csv extension, the file type is automatically recognized.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	is	You will see the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialog. Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255				0	is	If the csv file contains formulas, but you want to import the results of those formulas, then choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154022				0	is	To Export Formulas and Values as CSV Files				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	is	Click the sheet to be written as a csv file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3166423				0	is	If you want to export the formulas as formulas, for example, in the form =SUM(A1:B5), proceed as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155111				0	is	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150200				0	is	Under \<emph\>Display\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	is	If you want to export the calculation results instead of the formulas, do not mark \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3148702				0	is	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Save as\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153912				0	is	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File type\</item\> field select the format "Text CSV".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3157978				0	is	Enter a name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	is	From the \<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\> dialog that appears, select the character set and the field and text delimiters for the data to be exported, and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3146781				0	is	If the numbers use commas as decimal separators or thousands separators, do not select the comma as the field delimiter. If the text contains double quotation marks, you must select the single quotation mark as separator.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150050				0	is	If necessary, after you have saved, clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box to see the calculated results in the table again.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153487				0	is	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153008				0	is	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"Flytja út textaskrár\"\>Flytja út textaskrár\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155595				0	is	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Flytja inn textaskrár\"\>Flytja inn textaskrár\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Inserting and Editing Comments				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153968				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>comments; on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;comments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>remarks on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>viewing;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>displaying; comments\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968				0	is	\<variable id=\"note_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/note_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Comments\"\>Inserting and Editing Comments\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150440				0	is	You can assign a comment to each cell by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Comment\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Comment\</emph\>\</link\>. The comment is indicated by a small red square, the comment indicator, in the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	is	The comment is visible whenever the mouse pointer is over the cell, provided you have activated \<emph\>Help - Tips\</emph\> or - \<emph\>Extended Tips\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	is	When you select the cell, you can choose \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\> from the context menu of the cell. Doing so keeps the comment visible until you deactivate the \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\> command from the same context menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	is	To edit a permanently visible comment, just click in it. If you delete the entire text of the comment, the comment itself is deleted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN10699				0	is	Move or resize each comment as you like.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	is	Format each comment by specifying background color, transparency, border style, and text alignment. Choose the commands from the context menu of the comment.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	is	To show or hide the comment indicator, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and mark or unmark the \<emph\>Comment indicator\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	is	To display a help tip for a selected cell, use \<emph\>Data - Validity - Input Help\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	is	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Setja inn - Athugasemd\"\>Setja inn - Athugasemd\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Naming Cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147434				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>cells; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>names; defining for cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>values; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>constants definition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>variables; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell ranges; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;names for cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>addressing; by defined names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell names; defining/addressing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references; by defined names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>allowed cell names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>renaming;cells\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434				0	is	\<variable id=\"value_with_name\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/value_with_name.xhp\" name=\"Naming Cells\"\>Naming Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	hd_id4391918				0	is	Allowed names				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id2129581				0	is	Names in Calc can contain letters, numeric characters, and some special characters. Names must start with a letter or an underline character.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id1120029				0	is	Allowed special characters:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3362224				0	is	undirstrikun (_) 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id4891506				0	is	period (.) - allowed within a name, but not as first or last character				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id2816553				0	is	blank ( ) - allowed within a name, but not as first or last character, and not for a cell range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id328989				0	is	Names must not be the same as cell references. For example, the name A1 is invalid because A1 is a cell reference to the top left cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id32898987				0	is	Names must not start with the letter R followed by a number. See the ADDRESS function for more information.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id4769737				0	is	Names for cell ranges must not include blanks. Blanks are allowed within names for single cells, sheets and documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	hd_id1226233				0	is	Naming cells and formulas				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id5489364				0	is	A good way of making the references to cells and cell ranges in formulas legible is to give the ranges names. For example, you can name the range A1:B2 \<emph\>Start\</emph\>. You can then write a formula such as "=SUM(Start)". Even after you insert or delete rows or columns, $[officename] still correctly assigns the ranges identified by name. Range names must not contain any spaces.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id953398				0	is	For example, it is much easier to read a formula for sales tax if you can write "= Amount * Tax_rate" instead of "= A5 * B12". In this case, you would name cell A5 "Amount" and cell B12 "Tax_rate."				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id4889675				0	is	Use the \<emph\>Define Names\</emph\> dialog to define names for formulas or parts of formulas you need more often. In order to specify range names,				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3153954				0	is	Select a cell or range of cells, then choose \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Define Names\</emph\> dialog appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	is	Type the name of the selected area in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> field. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>. The newly defined name appears in the list below. Click OK to close the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id5774101				0	is	You can also name other cell ranges in this dialog by entering the name in the field and then selecting the respective cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942				0	is	If you type the name in a formula, after the first few characters entered you will see the entire name as a tip.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	is	Press the Enter key in order to accept the name from the tip.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	is	If more than one name starts with the same characters, you can scroll through all the names using the Tab key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	is	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04070100.xhp\" name=\"Setja inn - Nöfn - Skilgreina\"\>Setja inn - Nöfn - Skilgreina\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Calculating With Formulas				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>formulas;calculating with\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating; with formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples;formula calculation\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411				0	is	\<variable id=\"formulas\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formulas.xhp\" name=\"Calculating With Formulas\"\>Calculating With Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	is	All formulas begin with an equals sign. The formulas can contain numbers, text, arithmetic operators, logic operators, or functions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	is	Remember that the basic arithmetic operators (+, -, *, /) can be used in formulas using the "Multiplication and Division before Addition and Subtraction" rule. Instead of writing =SUM(A1:B1) you can write =A1+B1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	is	Parentheses can also be used. The result of the formula =(1+2)*3 produces a different result than =1+2*3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3156285				0	is	Here are a few examples of $[officename] Calc formulas:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154015				0	is	=A1+10				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972				0	is	Displays the contents of cell A1 plus 10.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3145643				0	is	=A1*16%				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	is	Displays 16% of the contents of A1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146917				0	is	=A1 * A2				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146315				0	is	Displays the result of the multiplication of A1 and A2.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	is	=ROUND(A1;1)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150363				0	is	Displays the contents of cell A1 rounded to one decimal place.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150209				0	is	=EFFECTIVE(5%;12)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150883				0	is	Calculates the effective interest for 5% annual nominal interest with 12 payments a year.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146114				0	is	=B8-SUM(B10:B14)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154486				0	is	Calculates B8 minus the sum of the cells B10 to B14.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3152890				0	is	=SUM(B8;SUM(B10:B14))				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3159171				0	is	Calculates the sum of cells B10 to B14 and adds the value to B8.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150109				0	is	It is also possible to nest functions in formulas, as shown in the example. You can also nest functions within functions. The Function Wizard assists you with nested functions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	is	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060100.xhp\" name=\"Functions list\"\>Functions list\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	is	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"Sjálfstýring: Föll\"\>Fallagerðarpúki\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148663				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; preventing data overwriting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>output ranges of pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148663				0	is	\<variable id=\"datapilot_tipps\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_tipps.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges\"\>Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	is	Click the button \<emph\>More\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialog. The dialog will be extended.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	is	You can select a named range in which the pivot table is to be created, from the \<emph\>Results to\</emph\> box. If the results range does not have a name, enter the coordinates of the upper left cell of the range into the field to the right of the \<emph\>Results to\</emph\> box. You can also click on the appropriate cell to have the coordinates entered accordingly.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	is	If you mark the \<emph\>Ignore empty rows\</emph\> check box, they will not be taken into account when the pivot table is created.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	is	If the \<emph\>Identify categories\</emph\> check box is marked, the categories will be identified by their headings and assigned accordingly when the pivot table is created.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Navigating Through Sheets Tabs				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; showing multiple\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheet tabs;using\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>views;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769	4			0	is	\<variable id=\"multi_tables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multi_tables.xhp\" name=\"Navigating Through Sheet Tabs\"\>Navigating Through Sheet Tabs\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	is	By default $[officename] displays three sheets "Sheet1" to "Sheet3", in each new spreadsheet. You can switch between sheets in a spreadsheet using the sheet tabs at the bottom of the screen.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	is	 \<image id=\"img_id4829822\" src=\"res/helpimg/sheettabs.png\" width=\"3.3335inch\" height=\"0.7638inch\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4829822\"\>Sheet Tabs\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	is	 \<image id=\"img_id3156441\" src=\"res/helpimg/calcnav.png\" width=\"0.6563inch\" height=\"0.1457inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156441\"\>Táknmynd\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	is	Use the navigation buttons to display all the sheets belonging to your document. Clicking the button on the far left or the far right displays, respectively, the first or last sheet tab. The middle buttons allow the user to scroll forward and backward through all sheet tabs. To display the sheet itself click on the sheet tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	is	If there is insufficient space to display all the sheet tabs, you can increase it by pointing to the separator between the scrollbar and the sheet tabs, pressing the mouse button and, keeping the mouse button pressed, dragging to the right. In doing so you will be sharing the available space between the sheet tabs and horizontal scrollbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Slá inn gildi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150868				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>values; inserting in multiple cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;values\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell ranges;selecting for data entries\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>areas, see also cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3405255				0	is	\<variable id=\"cell_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_enter.xhp\"\>Slá inn gildi\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7147129				0	is	Calc can simplify entering data and values into multiple cells. You can change some settings to conform to your preferences.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id5621509				0	is	To Enter Values Into a Range of Cells Manually				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8200018				0	is	There are two features that assist you when you enter a block of data manually.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id1867427				0	is	Area Detection for New Rows				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7908871				0	is	In the row below a heading row, you can advance from one cell to the next with the Tab key. After you enter the value into the last cell in the current row, press Enter. Calc positions the cursor below the first cell of the current block.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id6196783				0	is	\<image id=\"img_id6473586\" src=\"res/helpimg/area1.png\" width=\"4.8335in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6473586\"\>area detection\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8118839				0	is	In row 3, press Tab to advance from cell B3 to C3, D3, and E3. Then press Enter to advance to B4.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3583788				0	is	Val svæðis				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id2011780				0	is	Use drag-and-drop to select the area where you want to input values. But start dragging from the last cell of the area and release the mouse button when you have selected the first cell. Now you can start to input values. Always press the Tab key to advance to the next cell. You will not leave the selected area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7044282				0	is	\<image id=\"img_id2811365\" src=\"res/helpimg/area2.png\" width=\"4.8335in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2811365\"\>area selection\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3232520				0	is	Select the area from E7 to B3. Now B3 is waiting for your input. Press Tab to advance to the next cell within the selected area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id8950163				0	is	To Enter Values to a Range of Cells Automatically				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id633869				0	is	See \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_series.xhp\"\>Automatically Filling in Data Based on Adjacent Cells\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Rotating Tables (Transposing)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>tables; transposing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>transposing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inverting tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>swapping tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; swap with rows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; swapping with columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; rotating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rotating; tables\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	is	\<variable id=\"table_rotate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/table_rotate.xhp\" name=\"Rotating Tables (Transposing)\"\>Rotating Tables (Transposing)\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	is	In $[officename] Calc, there is a way to "rotate" a spreadsheet so that rows become columns and columns become rows.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	is	Select the cell range that you want to transpose.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153191				0	is	Veldu \<emph\>Breyta - Klippa\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	is	Click the cell that is to be the top left cell in the result.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	is	Veldu \<emph\>Breyta - Sérstök líming\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	is	In the dialog, mark \<emph\>Paste all\</emph\> and \<emph\>Transpose\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	is	If you now click OK the columns and rows are transposed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	is	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\" name=\"Sérstök líming\"\>Sérstök líming\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Printing Sheets in Landscape Format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153418				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheet selections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing in landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing; landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>landscape printing\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418				0	is	\<variable id=\"print_landscape\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_landscape.xhp\" name=\"Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\"\>Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149257				0	is	In order to print a sheet you have a number of interactive options available under \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>. Drag the delimiter lines to define the range of printed cells on each page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	is	To print in landscape format, proceed as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	is	Go to the sheet to be printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150786				0	is	Veldu \<emph\>Sníða - Síða \</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150089	5			0	is	The command is not visible if the sheet has been opened with write protection on. In that case, click the \<emph\>Edit File \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3166430				0	is	Select the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab. Select the \<emph\>Landscape\</emph\> paper format and click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150885				0	is	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3156288				0	is	Depending on the printer driver and the operating system, it may be necessary to click the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> button and to change your printer to landscape format there.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404	9			0	is	In the \<emph\>Print \</emph\>dialog in the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page, select the contents to be printed:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305	10			0	is	               \<emph\>All sheets\</emph\> - All sheets will be printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3148871	12			0	is	               \<emph\>Selected sheets\</emph\> - Only the selected sheets will be printed. All sheets whose names (at the bottom on the sheet tabs) are selected will be printed. By pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while clicking a sheet name you can change this selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3764763				0	is	               \<emph\>Selected cells\</emph\> - All selected cells are printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id5538804				0	is	From all the paper pages that result from the above selection, you can select the range of paper pages to be printed:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id14343				0	is	               \<emph\>All pages\</emph\> - Print all resulting pages.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3148699	11			0	is	               \<emph\>Pages\</emph\> - Enter the pages to be printed. The pages will also be numbered from the first sheet onwards. If you see in the Page Break Preview that Sheet1 will be printed on 4 pages and you want to print the first two pages of Sheet2, enter 5-6 here.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3145076				0	is	If under \<emph\>Format - Print ranges\</emph\> you have defined one or more print ranges, only the contents of these print ranges will be printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3156019				0	is	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"Skoða - Forskoðun síðuskila\"\>Skoða - Forskoðun síðuskila\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id8254646				0	is	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/printranges.xhp\"\>Defining Print Ranges on a Sheet\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155686				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; moving cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; moving by drag and drop \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns;moving by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;cells by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;cells, by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id986358				0	is	\<variable id=\"move_dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/move_dragdrop.xhp\"\>Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2760093				0	is	When you drag-and-drop a selection of cells on a Calc sheet, the cells normally overwrite the existing cells in the area where you drop. This is the normal \<emph\>overwrite mode\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9527268				0	is	When you hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while releasing the mouse button, you enter the \<emph\>insert mode\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id79653				0	is	In insert mode, the existing cells where you drop will be shifted to the right or to the bottom, and the dropped cells are inserted into the now empty positions without overwriting. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8676717				0	is	The surrounding box of the moved cells looks different in insert mode. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3968932				0	is	In overwrite mode you see all four borders around the selected area. In insert mode you see only the left border when target cells will be shifted to the right. You see only the upper border when target cells will be shifted down. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id7399517				0	is	Whether the target area will be shifted to the right or to the bottom depends on the distance between source and target cells, if you move within the same sheet. It depends on the number of horizontal or vertical cells in the moved area, if you move to a different sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8040406				0	is	If you move cells in insert mode within the same row (only horizontally), then after insertion of the cells, all cells will be shifted to the left to fill the source area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2586748				0	is	In both modes, you can hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key, or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys while you release the mouse button to insert a copy or a link, respectively.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5814081				0	is	Keys pressed while releasing the mouse button				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6581316				0	is	Útkoma				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9906613				0	is	Engir hnappar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2815637				0	is	Cells are moved and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells are emptied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6161687				0	is	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Val \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>lykill				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4278389				0	is	Cells are copied and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2805566				0	is	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Val\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift lyklar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5369121				0	is	Links to the source cells are inserted and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				20181231 09:50:43
