helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10756				0	is	You can open and save data in the dBASE file format (*.dbf file extension) in $[officename] Base or a spreadsheet. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, a dBASE database is a folder that contains files with the .dbf file extension. Each file corresponds to a table in the database. Formulas and formatting are lost when you open and save a dBASE file from %PRODUCTNAME.				20181231 09:50:43
