helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154208				0	is	Dæmi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150777				0	is	A die is thrown 1020 times. The numbers on the die 1 through 6 come up 195, 151, 148, 189, 183 and 154 times (observation values). The hypothesis that the die is not fixed is to be tested.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3153062				0	is	The Chi square distribution of the random sample is determined by the formula given above. Since the expected value for a given number on the die for n throws is n times 1/6, thus 1020/6 = 170, the formula returns a Chi square value of 13.27.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148806				0	is	If the (observed) Chi square is greater than or equal to the (theoretical) Chi square CHIINV, the hypothesis will be discarded, since the deviation between theory and experiment is too great. If the observed Chi square is less that CHIINV, the hypothesis is confirmed with the indicated probability of error.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	95			0	is	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=CHIINV(0.05;5)\</item\> skilar 11.07.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3159142	133			0	is	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=CHIINV(0.02;5)\</item\> skilar 13.39.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3158401				0	is	If the probability of error is 5%, the die is not true. If the probability of error is 2%, there is no reason to believe it is fixed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154260				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>CHITEST fall\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
