helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149566	9			0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_FORMULA:BTN_MATRIX\"\>Specifies that the selected function is inserted into the selected cell range as an array formula. \</ahelp\> Array formulas operate on multiple cells. Each cell in the array contains the formula, not as a copy but as a common formula shared by all matrix cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	is	The \<emph\>Array\</emph\> option is identical to the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+Enter command, which is used to enter and confirm formulas in the sheet. The formula is inserted as a matrix formula indicated by two braces { }.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993				0	is	The maximum size of an array range is 128 by 128 cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150367				0	is	Argument Input Fields				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	is	When you double-click a function, the argument input field(s) appear on the right side of the dialog. To select a cell reference as an argument, click directly into the cell, or drag across the required range on the sheet while holding down the mouse button. You can also enter numerical and other values or references directly into the corresponding fields in the dialog. When using \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060102.xhp\" name=\"date entries\"\>date entries\</link\>, make sure you use the correct format. Click OK to insert the result into the spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149408				0	is	Útkoma falls				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155809				0	is	As soon you enter arguments in the function, the result is calculated. This preview informs you if the calculation can be carried out with the arguments given. If the arguments result in an error, the corresponding \<link href=\"text/scalc/05/02140000.xhp\" name=\"error code\"\>error code\</link\> is displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148700				0	is	The required arguments are indicated by names in bold print.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153064				0	is	f(x) (depending on the selected function)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3157980				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_FAP_BTN_FX4\"\>Allows you to access a subordinate level of the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> in order to nest another function within the function, instead of a value or reference.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145076				0	is	Argument/Parameter/Cell Reference (depending on the selected function)				20181231 09:50:43
