helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148801				0	is	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is a constant. The interest rate is to be calculated for the entire duration (duration period). The interest rate per period is calculated by dividing the interest rate by the calculated duration. The internal rate for an annuity is to be entered as Rate/12.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147239				0	is	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present (current) value. The cash value is the deposit of cash or the current cash value of an allowance in kind. As a deposit value a positive value must be entered; the deposit must not be 0 or <0.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147515				0	is	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> is the expected value. The future value determines the desired (future) value of the deposit.				20181231 09:50:43
