helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_id3149770				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KALENDERWOCHE\"\>WEEKNUM calculates the week number of the year for the internal date value.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E4				0	is	The International Standard ISO 8601 has decreed that Monday shall be the first day of the week. A week that lies partly in one year and partly in another is assigned a number in the year in which most of its days lie. That means that week number 1 of any year is the week that contains the January 4th.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153055				0	is	Notkun				20181231 09:50:43
