helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148981				0	is	Dæmi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155904				0	is	In the following table, column A lists unsorted measurement values. Column B contains the upper limit you entered for the classes into which you want to divide the data in column A. According to the limit entered in B1, the FREQUENCY function returns the number of measured values less than or equal to 5. As the limit in B2 is 10, the FREQUENCY function returns the second result as the number of measured values that are greater than 5 and less than or equal to 10. The text you entered in B6, ">25", is only for reference purposes.				20181231 09:50:43
