helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150313				0	is	\<emph\>Count1\</emph\> is the number of items in the set.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153830				0	is	\<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of items to choose from the set.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6807458				0	is	COMBIN returns the number of ordered ways to choose these items. For example if there are 3 items A, B and C in a set, you can choose 2 items in 3 different ways, namely AB, AC and BC.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7414471				0	is	COMBIN implements the formula: Count1!/(Count2!*(Count1-Count2)!)				20181231 09:50:43
