helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153372				0	is	\<emph\>Count1\</emph\> is the number of items in the set.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155544				0	is	\<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of items to choose from the set.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1997131				0	is	COMBINA returns the number of unique ways to choose these items, where the order of choosing is irrelevant, and repetition of items is allowed. For example if there are 3 items A, B and C in a set, you can choose 2 items in 6 different ways, namely AA, AB, AC, BB, BC and CC.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2052064				0	is	COMBINA implements the formula: (Count1+Count2-1)! / (Count2!(Count1-1)!)				20181231 09:50:43
