helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154735				0	is	Settlement date: February 15 1999, maturity date: May 15 1999, investment sum: 1000 currency units, discount: 5.75 per cent, basis: Daily balance/360 = 2.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146108				0	is	The amount received on the maturity date is calculated as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147246	401			0	is	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=RECEIVED("1999-02-15";"1999-05-15";1000;0.0575;2)\</item\> returns 1014.420266.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147556				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>PV function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>present values\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>calculating; present values\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147556				0	is	PV				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153301				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_BW\"\>Returns the present value of an investment resulting from a series of regular payments.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146099				0	is	Use this function to calculate the amount of money needed to be invested at a fixed rate today, to receive a specific amount, an annuity, over a specified number of periods. You can also determine how much money is to remain after the elapse of the period. Specify as well if the amount is to be paid out at the beginning or at the end of each period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153334				0	is	Enter these values either as numbers, expressions or references. If, for example, interest is paid annually at 8%, but you want to use month as your period, enter 8%/12 under \<emph\>Rate\</emph\> and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc with automatically calculate the correct factor.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147407				0	is	Notkun				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150395				0	is	PV(Rate; NPer; Pmt; FV; Type)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3151341	9			0	is	            \<emph\>Rate\</emph\> defines the interest rate per period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153023	10			0	is	            \<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of periods (payment period).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146323	11			0	is	            \<emph\>Pmt\</emph\> is the regular payment made per period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150536	12			0	is	            \<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) defines the future value remaining after the final installment has been made.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146883	13			0	is	            \<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) denotes due date for payments. Type = 1 means due at the beginning of a period and Type = 0 (default) means due at the end of the period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B13				0	is	            \<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>         				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150037				0	is	Dæmi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145225				0	is	What is the present value of an investment, if 500 currency units are paid out monthly and the annual interest rate is 8%? The payment period is 48 months and 20,000 currency units are to remain at the end of the payment period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907	16			0	is	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=PV(8%/12;48;500;20000)\</item\> = -35,019.37 currency units. Under the named conditions, you must deposit 35,019.37 currency units today, if you want to receive 500 currency units per month for 48 months and have 20,000 currency units left over at the end. Cross-checking shows that 48 x 500 currency units + 20,000 currency units = 44,000 currency units. The difference between this amount and the 35,000 currency units deposited represents the interest paid.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149150				0	is	If you enter references instead of these values into the formula, you can calculate any number of "If-then" scenarios. Please note: references to constants must be defined as absolute references. Examples of this type of application are found under the depreciation functions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152978				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; depreciations\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>SYD function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>depreciations; arithmetic declining\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>arithmetic declining depreciations\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152978				0	is	SYD				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148732				0	is	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DIA\"\>Returns the arithmetic-declining depreciation rate.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149886				0	is	Use this function to calculate the depreciation amount for one period of the total depreciation span of an object. Arithmetic declining depreciation reduces the depreciation amount from period to period by a fixed sum.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149431				0	is	Notkun				20181231 09:50:43
