helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	is	Input: Function number between 0 and nCount-1, inclusively.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149546				0	is	char* pFuncName:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148579	52			0	is	Output: Function name as seen by the programmer, as it is named in the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. This name does not determine the name used in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153935				0	is	USHORT& nParamCount:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150142				0	is	Output: Number of parameters in AddIn function. This number must be greater than 0, because there is always a result value; the maximum value is 16.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3145143				0	is	Paramtype* peType:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148750				0	is	Output: Pointer to an array of exactly 16 variables of type Paramtype. The first nParamCount entries are filled with the suitable type of parameter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153078				0	is	char* pInternalName:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3155261				0	is	Output: Function name as seen by the user, as it appears in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>. May contain umlauts.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153327				0	is	The pFuncName and pInternalName parameters are char arrays, which are implemented with size 256 in $[officename] Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148567				0	is	GetParameterDescription()				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153000				0	is	Provides a brief description of the Add-In function and its parameters. As an option, this function can be used to show a function and parameter description in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154501				0	is	\<emph\>Notkun\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153564				0	is	void CALLTYPE GetParameterDescription(USHORT& nNo, USHORT& nParam, char* pName, char* pDesc)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3157995				0	is	\<emph\>Viðfang\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3155925				0	is	USHORT& nNo:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149883				0	is	Input: Number of the function in the library; between 0 and nCount-1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154326				0	is	USHORT& nParam:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3159139				0	is	Input: Indicates, for which parameter the description is provided; parameters start at 1. If nParam is 0, the description itself is supposed to be provided in pDesc; in this case, pName does not have any meaning.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3147374				0	is	char* pName:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3145245				0	is	Output: Takes up the parameter name or type, for example, the word "Number" or "String" or "Date", and so on. Implemented in $[officename] Calc as char[256].				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3151020				0	is	char* pDesc:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148389				0	is	Output: Takes up the description of the parameter, for example, "Value, at which the universe is to be calculated." Implemented in $[officename] Calc as char[256].				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3145303				0	is	pName and pDesc are char arrays; implemented in $[officename] Calc with size 256. Please note that the space available in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> is limited and that the 256 characters cannot be fully used.				20181231 09:50:43
