helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154570				0	is	The direct cursor allows you to click in any blank area of a page to place text, images, tables, frames, and other objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902				0	is	If you place the direct cursor approximately in the middle between the left and the right margin of a page or a table cell, the text you insert will be centered. Similarly, text is right-aligned when the direct cursor is placed on the right margin.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151255				0	is	The AutoCorrect tool automatically removes empty paragraphs, tabs, and spaces that are inserted by the direct cursor. If you want to use the direct cursor, then disable the AutoCorrect tool.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148982				0	is	The direct cursor sets tabs to position the cursor. If you change the tabs later. the position of the text on the page may change as well.				20181231 09:50:43
