helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Skilyrtur texti				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155619				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>matching conditional text in fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>if-then queries as fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>conditional text; setting up\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; conditional text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;conditions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155619				0	is	\<variable id=\"conditional_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/conditional_text.xhp\" name=\"Skilyrtur texti\"\>Skilyrtur texti\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879				0	is	You can set up fields in your document that display text when a condition that you define is met. For example, you can define the conditional text that is displayed in a series of reminder letters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	is	Setting up conditional text in this example is a two-part process. First you create a variable, and then you create the condition.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153175				0	is	To Define a Conditional Variable				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153185	62			0	is	The first part of the example is to define a variable for the condition statement. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155566				0	is	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Variables\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147759				0	is	Click "Set variable" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147784				0	is	Type a name for the variable in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Name\</item\> box, for example \<item type=\"literal\"\>Reminder\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147810				0	is	Click "Text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id7748344				0	is	Enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>.\<br/\>The Format list now displays a "General" format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145645				0	is	To Define a Condition and the Conditional Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145659				0	is	The second part of the example is to define the condition that must be met, and to insert a placeholder for displaying the conditional text in your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151193				0	is	Place the cursor where you want to insert the conditional text in your text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212				0	is	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250				0	is	Click "Conditional text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155936				0	is	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Reminder EQ "3"\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. In other words, the conditional text will be displayed when the variable in the field that you defined in the first part of this example is equal to three.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155969				0	is	The quotation marks enclosing the "3" indicate that the variable that you defined in the first part of this example is a text string.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150446				0	is	Type the text that you want to display when the condition is met in the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box. There is almost no limit to the length of the text that you can enter. You can paste a paragraph into this box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150473				0	is	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155073				0	is	To Display the Conditional Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155086				0	is	In this example, the conditional text is displayed when the value of the conditional variable is equal to 3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155110				0	is	Place your cursor in front of the field that you defined in the first part of this example, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	is	Replace the number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box with 3, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155168				0	is	If the field does not automatically update, press F9.				20181231 09:50:43
