helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200916345516				0	is	Wildcards or placeholders can be used to search for some unspecified or even invisible characters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182				0	is	You can use wildcards when you find and replace text in a document. For example, "s.n" finds "sun" and "son".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	is	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Find & Replace\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id2142399				0	is	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>More Options\</item\> to expand the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	is	Select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Regular expressions\</item\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843				0	is	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for\</item\> box, type the search term and the wildcard(s) that you want to use in your search.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	is	Smelltu á \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Leita\</item\> eða \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Finna allt\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153401				0	is	Regular Expression Examples				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	is	The wildcard for a single character is a period (.).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153136				0	is	The wildcard for zero or more occurrences of the previous character is an asterisk. For example: "123*" finds "12" "123", and "1233".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149609				0	is	The wildcard combination to search for zero or more occurrences of any character is a period and asterisk (.*).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149854				0	is	The wildcard for the end of a paragraph is a dollar sign ($). The wildcard character combination for the start of a paragraph is a caret and a period (^.).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200916345545				0	is	The wildcard for a tab character is \\t.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	is	A search using a regular expression will work only within one paragraph. To search using a regular expression in more than one paragraph, do a separate search in each paragraph.				20181231 09:50:43
