helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6111941				0	is	Now you want some more control on page numbers. You are writing a text document that should start with page number 12.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5757621				0	is	Click into the first paragraph of your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2632831				0	is	Veldu \<emph\>Sníða - Málsgrein - Textaflæði\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4395275				0	is	In the Breaks area, enable \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. Enable \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\> just to be able to set the new \<emph\>Page number\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1654408				0	is	The new page number is an attribute of the first paragraph of the page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id7519150				0	is	To Format the Page Number Style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id9029206				0	is	You want roman page numbers running i, ii, iii, iv, and so on.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3032319				0	is	Double-click directly before the page number field. You see the \<emph\>Edit Fields\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id9139378				0	is	Select a number format and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id5051728				0	is	Using Different Page Number Styles				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1558885				0	is	You need some pages with the roman numbering style, followed by the remaining pages in another style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1541184				0	is	In Writer, you will need different page styles. The first page style has a footer with a page number field formatted for roman numbers. The following page style has a footer with a page number field formatted in another look.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id18616				0	is	Both page styles must be separated by a page break. In Writer, you can have automatic page breaks and manually inserted page breaks.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6138492				0	is	An \<emph\>automatic page break\</emph\> appears at the end of a page when the page style has a different "next style".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4569231				0	is	For example, the "First Page" page style has "Default" as the next style. To see this, you may press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+T\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>F11\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> to open the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles and Formatting\</item\> window, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> icon, right-click the First Page entry. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify\</item\> from the context menu. On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab, you can see the "next style".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id291451				0	is	A \<emph\>manually inserted page break\</emph\> can be applied without or with a change of page styles.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3341776				0	is	If you just press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\>, you apply a page break without a change of styles.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5947141				0	is	If you choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual break\</emph\>, you can insert a page break without or with a change of style or with a change of page number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1911679				0	is	It depends on your document what is best: to use a manually inserted page break between page styles, or to use an automatic change. If you just need one title page with a different style than the other pages, you can use the automatic method:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id9364909				0	is	To Apply a Different Page Style to the First Page				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4473403				0	is	Click into the first page of your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4313791				0	is	Veldu \<emph\>Sníða - Stílar og snið\</emph\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	is	In the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4191717				0	is	Double-click the "First Page" style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2318796				0	is	Now your title page has the style "First Page", and the next pages automatically have the "Default" style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id399182				0	is	You can now for example insert a footer for the "Default" page atyle only, or insert footers in both page styles, but with differently formatted page number fields.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id5298318				0	is	To Apply a Manually Inserted Page Style Change				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id7588732				0	is	Click at the start of the first paragraph on the page where a different page style will be applied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id95828				0	is	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>. You see the \<emph\>Insert Break\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3496200				0	is	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> list box, select a page style. You may set a new page number, too. Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id7599108				0	is	The selected page style will be used from the current paragraph to the next page break with style. You may need to create the new page style first.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	About Headers and Footers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155863				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>headers;about\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers;about\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; headers and footers\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	is	\<variable id=\"header_footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_footer.xhp\" name=\"About Headers and Footers\"\>About Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	is	Headers and footers are areas in the top and the bottom page margins, where you can add text or graphics. Headers and footers are added to the current page style. Any page that uses the same style automatically receives the header or footer that you add. You can insert \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\>, such as page numbers and chapter headings, in headers and footers in a text document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150511				0	is	The page style for the current page is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	is	To add a header to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147119				0	is	To add a footer to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	is	You can also choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page\</item\>, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footer\</item\> tab, and then select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header on\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footer on\</item\>. Clear the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Same content left/right\</item\> check box if you want to define different headers and footers for even and odd pages.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3146876				0	is	To use different headers or footers in your document, you must add them to different \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>, and then apply the styles to the pages where you want the headers or footer to appear.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150704				0	is	Headers and Footers in HTML Documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	34			0	is	Some of the header and footer options are also available for HTML documents. Headers and footers are not supported by HTML and instead are exported with special tags, so that they can be viewed in a browser. Headers and footers are only exported in HTML documents if they are enabled in Web Layout mode. When you reopen the document in $[officename], the headers and footers are displayed correctly, including any fields that you inserted. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153174				0	is	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Síðustílar\"\>Síðustílar\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Spacing Between Footnotes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147683				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>spacing; endnotes/footnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>endnotes; spacing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footnotes; spacing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders;for footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines;footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
