helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149909				0	is	\<variable id=\"calculate\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate.xhp\" name=\"Calculating in Text Documents\"\>Calculating in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	is	You can insert a calculation directly into a text document or into a text table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149972				0	is	Click in the document where you want to insert the calculation, and then press F2. If you are in a table cell, type an equals sign =.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155547				0	is	Type the calculation that you want to insert, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=10000/12\</item\>, and then press Enter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155565				0	is	You can also click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula\</item\> icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\>, and then choose a function for your formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id8316904				0	is	To reference cells in a Writer text table, enclose the cell address or the cell range in angle brackets. For example, to reference cell A1 from another cell, enter =<A1> into the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Using Smart Tags				20181231 09:50:43
