helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155174	30			0	is	\<variable id=\"using_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Numbering and Numbering Styles\"\>Numbering and Numbering Styles\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149818				0	is	You can apply numbering to a paragraph manually or with a paragraph style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id6140629				0	is	To Apply Numbering Manually				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155866				0	is	To apply numbering manually, click in the paragraph, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering On/Off\</item\> icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> Bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3153405				0	is	You cannot apply manual numbering to paragraphs that are listed under "Special Styles" in the Styles and Formatting window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN10711				0	is	When you press Enter in a numbered or bulleted list, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> automatically numbers the next paragraph. To remove the numbering or bullet from the new paragraph, press Enter again.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072B				0	is	To change the hierarchical level of a bullet in a list, click in front of the paragraph, then press the Tab key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072F				0	is	To change the bullets or numbering format for the current paragraph only, select a character or word in the paragraph, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</item\>, and then click a new format. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN10733				0	is	To change the bullet or numbering format for all paragraphs in the list, ensure that the cursor is in the list, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</item\>, and then click a new format. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN10737				0	is	To apply the same bullet or numbering format to all paragraphs in the list, select all paragraphs, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</item\>, and then click a format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073A				0	is	You can also use the commands on the \<link href=\"text/swriter/main0206.xhp\" name=\"Numbering Object Bar\"\>Bullets and Numbering\</link\> toolbar to edit a numbered or bulleted list. To change the numbering or bullet format, click the \<emph\>Bullets and Numbering\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153123				0	is	To Apply Numbering With a Paragraph Style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3153137				0	is	Paragraph Styles give you greater control over numbering that you apply in a document. When you change the numbering format of the style, all paragraphs using the style are automatically updated.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149646				0	is	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paragraph Styles\</item\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149599				0	is	Right-click the paragraph style that you want to apply numbering to, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149850				0	is	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Outline & Numbering\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874				0	is	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering Style\</item\> box, select the type of numbering that you want to use.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3145113				0	is	Smelltu á \<emph\>Í lagi\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149589				0	is	Apply the style to the paragraphs that you want to add numbering to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Modifying Rows and Columns by Keyboard				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155856				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>table mode selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>proportional distribution of tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative distribution of table cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; adapting the width by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; adapting the width by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keyboard;modifying the behavior of rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>behavior of rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155856				0	is	\<variable id=\"tablemode\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/tablemode.xhp\" name=\"Modifying the Behavior of Rows and Columns for Table\"\>Modifying Rows and Columns by Keyboard\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149835				0	is	When you insert or delete cells, rows or columns in a table, the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Behavior of rows/columns\</item\> options determine how the neighboring elements are affected. For example, you can only insert new rows and columns into a table with fixed row and column dimensions if space permits.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id7344279				0	is	Note that these properties are valid only for changes to the column width that are made using the keyboard. Using the mouse, you are free to make any column width changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3156110				0	is	To set the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Behavior of rows/columns\</item\> options for tables in text documents, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</item\>, or use the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Fixed\</item\>, \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Fixed/Proportional\</item\>, and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Variable\</item\> icons on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table\</item\> Bar. There are three display modes for tables:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149638				0	is	\<emph\>Fixed\</emph\> - changes only affect the adjacent cell, and not the entire table. For example, when you widen a cell, the adjacent cell becomes narrower, but the width of the table remains constant.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149613				0	is	\<emph\>Fixed, proportional\</emph\> - changes affect the entire table, and wide cells shrink more than narrow cells. For example, when you widen a cell, the adjacent cells become proportionally narrower, but the width of the table remains constant.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149864				0	is	\<emph\>Variable\</emph\> - changes affect the table size. For example, when you widen a cell, the width of the table increases.				20181231 09:50:43
