helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	is	A template is a document that contains specific formatting styles, graphics, tables, objects, and other information. A template is used as the basis for creating other documents. For example, you can define paragraph and character styles in a document, save the document as a template, and then use the template to create a new document with the same styles.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149957				0	is	Unless you specify otherwise, every new $[officename] text document is based on the default template.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149974				0	is	$[officename] has a number of \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"predefined templates\"\>predefined templates\</link\> that you can use to create different types or text documents, such as business letters.				20181231 09:50:43
