helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151355				0	is	You can store AutoText entries in different directories on a network.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370				0	is	For example, you can store "read-only" AutoText entries for your company on a central server, and user-defined AutoText entries in a local directory.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	is	The paths for the AutoText directories can be edited in the configuration.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154960				0	is	Two directories are listed here. The first entry is on the server installation and the second entry is in the user directory. If there are two AutoText entries with the same name in both directories, the entry from the user directory is used.				20181231 09:50:43
