helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153407				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>page styles; left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>blank pages with alternating page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>empty page with alternating page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages; left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; even/odd pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>title pages; page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>First Page page style\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Left Page page style\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>even/odd pages;formatting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153407				0	is	\<variable id=\"even_odd_sdw\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/even_odd_sdw.xhp\" name=\"Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\"\>Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154265				0	is	\<image id=\"img_id3155876\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_designerdialog.png\" width=\"0.1862in\" height=\"0.1862in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155876\"\>Táknmynd\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147126				0	is	$[officename] can automatically apply alternating page styles on even (left) and odd pages (right) in your document. For example, you can use page styles to display different headers and footers on even and odd pages. The current page style is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\> at the bottom of the workplace.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id8194219				0	is	To Set Up Alternating Page Styles				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150526				0	is	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153				0	is	In the list of page styles, right-click "Left Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153179				0	is	Smelltu á \<emph\>Skipulag\</emph\> flipann.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145267				0	is	Select "Right Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145299				0	is	In the list of page styles, right-click "Right Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	is	Select "Left Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155561				0	is	Go to the first page in your document, and double-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles in the Styles and Formatting window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155588				0	is	To add a header to one of the page styles, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Header\</item\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the header to. In the header frame, type the text that you want to use as the header.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147772				0	is	To add a footer to one of the page styles, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Footer\</item\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the footer to. In the footer frame, type the text that you want to use as a footer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	is	If you do not want to have a header or a footer on the title page of your document, apply the "First Page" style to the title page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id888698				0	is	To Suppress the Printout of Empty Pages				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3394573				0	is	If two even or two odd pages directly follow each other in your document, Writer will insert an empty page by default. You can suppress those automatically generated empty pages from printing and from exporting to PDF.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id7594225				0	is	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id8147221				0	is	Remove the check mark from \<emph\>Print automatically inserted blank pages\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145596				0	is	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04010000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Break dialog\"\>Insert Break dialog\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Changing Page Orientation (Landscape or Portrait)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	bm_id9683828				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>page styles;orientation/scope\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page formats; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>portrait and landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>landscape and portrait\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;portrait/landscape format\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paper orientation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages;orientation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sideways orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scope of page styles\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FF				0	is	\<variable id=\"pageorientation\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pageorientation.xhp\"\>Changing Page Orientation\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6418042				0	is	All page properties for Writer text documents, like for example the page orientation, are defined by page styles. By default, a new text document uses the “Default” page style for all pages. If you open an existing text document, different page styles may have been applied to the different pages. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id8324533				0	is	It is important to know that changes that you apply to a page property will only affect the pages that use the current page style. The current page style is listed in the Status Bar at the lower window border.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7524033				0	is	To Change the Page Orientation for All Pages				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6307260				0	is	If your text document consists only of pages with the same page style, you can change the page properties directly:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id5256508				0	is	Veldu \<emph\>Sníða - Síða \</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id9681997				0	is	Smelltu á \<emph\>Síðu\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7994323				0	is	Under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paper format\</item\>, select “Portrait” or “Landscape”.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7069002				0	is	Smelltu á \<emph\>Í lagi\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id4202398				0	is	To Change the Page Orientation Only for Some Pages				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	is	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the orientation of the pages in a document. Page styles define more page properties, as for example header and footer or page margins. You can either change the “Default” page style for the current document, or you can define own page styles and apply those page styles to any parts of your text. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1449324				0	is	At the end of this help page, we'll discuss the scope of page styles in detail. If you are unsure about the page style concept, please read the section at the end of this page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1480758				0	is	Unlike character styles or paragraph styles, the page styles don't know a hierarchy. You can create a new page style based on the properties of an existing page style, but when you later change the source style, the new page style does not automatically inherit the changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2962126				0	is	To change the page orientation for all pages that share the same page style, you first need a page style, then apply that style:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10727				0	is	Veldu \<emph\>Sníða - Stílar og snið\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10741				0	is	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	is	Right-click a page style and choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>. The new page style initially gets all properties of the selected page style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	is	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab page, type a name for the page style in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box, for example "My Landscape".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075D				0	is	In the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, select the page style that you want to apply to the next page that follows a page with the new style. See the section about the scope of page styles at the end of this help page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10775				0	is	Smelltu á \<emph\>Síðu\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077D				0	is	Under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paper format\</item\>, select “Portrait” or “Landscape”.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	is	Smelltu á \<emph\>Í lagi\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1658375				0	is	Now you have defined a proper page style with the name "My Landscape". To apply the new style, double-click the "My Landscape" page style in the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window. All pages in the current scope of page styles will be changed. If you defined the "next style" to be a different style, only the first page of the current scope of page styles will be changed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id6082949				0	is	The Scope of Page Styles				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2858668				0	is	You should be aware of the scope of page styles in %PRODUCTNAME. Which pages of your text document get affected by editing a page style?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3278603				0	is	One Page Long Styles				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id5169225				0	is	A page style can be defined to span one page only. The “First Page” style is an example. You set this property by defining another page style to be the "next style", on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Organizer\</item\> tab page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6670125				0	is	A one page long style starts from the lower border of the current page style range up to the next page break. The next page break appears automatically when the text flows to the next page, which is sometimes called a "soft page break". Alternatively, you can insert a manual page break.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2118594				0	is	To insert a manual page break at the cursor position, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\> or choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Manual Break\</item\> and just click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id166020				0	is	Manually Defined Range of a Page style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6386913				0	is	The “Default” page style does not set a different "next style" on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Organizer\</item\> tab page. Instead, the "next style" is set also to be “Default”. All page styles that are followed by the same page style can span multiple pages. The lower and upper borders of the page style range are defined by "page breaks with style". All the pages between any two "page breaks with style" use the same page style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6062196				0	is	You can insert a "page break with style" directly at the cursor position. Alternatively, you can apply the "page break with style" property to a paragraph or to a paragraph style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6054261				0	is	Perform any one of the following commands:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1811578				0	is	To insert a "page break with style" at the cursor position, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Manual Break\</item\>, select a \<emph\>Style\</emph\> name from the listbox, and click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id9935911				0	is	To apply the "page break with style" property to the current paragraph, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph - Text Flow\</item\>. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id4753868				0	is	To apply the "page break with style" property to the current paragraph style, right-click the current paragraph. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit Paragraph Style\</item\> from the context menu. Click the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id4744407				0	is	To apply the "page break with style" property to an arbitrary paragraph style, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>. Click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon. Right-click the name of the paragraph style you want to modify and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. Click the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	is	Indexes Covering Several Documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153418				0	is	\<bookmark_value\>indexes;multiple documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>multiple documents;indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>master documents;indexes\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418				0	is	\<variable id=\"indices_multidoc\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_multidoc.xhp\" name=\"Indexes Covering Several Documents\"\>Indexes Covering Several Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	is	There are several ways to create an index that spans several documents:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	is	Create an \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120210.xhp\" name=\"index in each individual document\"\>index in each individual document\</link\>, copy and paste the indexes into a single document, and then edit them.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3147118				0	is	Select each index, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Section\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Section\</item\>\</link\>, and then enter a name for the index. In a separate document, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Section\</item\>, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link\</item\>, click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>), and then locate and insert a named index section.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150230				0	is	Create a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010001.xhp\" name=\"master document\"\>master document\</link\>, add as subdocuments the files that you want to include in the index, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Index and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
