helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150147				0	is	For example, to hide a paragraph, text, or a section from a user with a specific initial, such as "LM", enter the condition: user_initials=="LM".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154115				0	is	Conditions and Database Fields				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154128				0	is	You can define conditions for accessing databases, or database fields. For example, you can check the contents of a database field from a condition, or use database fields in logical expressions. The following table lists a few more examples of using databases in conditions:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156066				0	is	Dæmi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156088				0	is	Þýðir				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155948				0	is	Database.Table.Company				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148673				0	is	Database.Table.Company NEQ ""				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148687				0	is	Database.Table.Company != ""				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155373				0	is	The condition is true if the COMPANY field is not empty. (In the first example, no operator is required.)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149977				0	is	!Database.Table.Company				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149991				0	is	NOT Database.Table.Company				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150004				0	is	Database.Table.Company EQ ""				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146911				0	is	Database.Table.Company ==""				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148733				0	is	Returns TRUE if the COMPANY field is empty.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148762				0	is	Database.Table.Company !="Sun"				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153016				0	is	Database.Table.Company NEQ "Sun"				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153040				0	is	Returns TRUE if the current entry in the COMPANY field is not "Sun". (Exclamation sign represents a logical NOT.)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154605				0	is	Database.Table.Firstname AND Database.Table.Name				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153059				0	is	Returns TRUE if the record contains the first and the last name.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159247				0	is	Note the difference between the boolean NOT "!" and the comparative operator not equal "!=" (NEQ).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	is	When you refer to a database field in a condition, use the form Databasename.Tablename.Fieldname. If one of the names contains a character that is an operator, such as a minus sign (-), enclose the name in square brackets, for example, Databasename.[Table-name].Fieldname. Never use spaces inside field names.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153891				0	is	Example: Hiding an Empty Database Field				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051				0	is	You may want to create a condition that hides an empty field, for example, if the COMPANY field is empty for some of the data records.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150067				0	is	Select the \<emph\>Hidden Paragraph\</emph\> list entry, and type the following condition: Addressbook.Addresses.Company EQ ""				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110				0	is	or type the following				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147123				0	is	NOT Addressbook.Addresses.Company				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147136				0	is	If the COMPANY database field is empty, the condition is true and the paragraph is hidden.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150232				0	is	To display hidden paragraphs on the screen, you can choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\>, and clear the \<emph\>Fields: Hidden paragraphs\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145218				0	is	Examples of Conditions in Fields				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145231				0	is	The following examples use the Conditional text field, although they can be applied to any fields that can be linked to a condition. The syntax used for conditions is also used for the Hidden text, Hidden paragraph, Any record or Next record fields.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150311				0	is	To display conditional text based on the number of pages:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150333				0	is	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147471				0	is	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, click "Conditional text".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154294	63			0	is	In the \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box, type "page == 1".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	is	In the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box, type "There is only one page".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150640	65			0	is	In the \<emph\>Or \</emph\>box, type "There are several pages".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153086				0	is	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155814				0	is	To display conditional text based on a user-defined Variable				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155836				0	is	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Variables\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155109	68			0	is	In the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list, click "Set Variable".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	139			0	is	In the\<emph\> Name\</emph\> box, type "Profit".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147032	140			0	is	In the\<emph\> Value\</emph\> box, type "5000".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152974				0	is	Smelltu á \<emph\>Setja inn\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152998				0	is	Click the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab, and click "Conditional text" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150952				0	is	In the \<emph\>Condition\</emph\> box, type "Profit < 5000".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156291				0	is	In the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box, type "Target is not met".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156317	72			0	is	In the \<emph\>Or \</emph\>box, type "Target is met".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	is	Smelltu á \<emph\>Setja inn\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154389				0	is	To edit the contents of the "Profit" variable, double-click the variable field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155573				0	is	To display conditional text based on the contents of a database field:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155587				0	is	The first part of this example inserts a space between the "First Name" and "Last Name" fields in a document, and the second part inserts text based on the contents of a field. This example requires that an address data source is registered with $[officename].				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150523				0	is	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Database\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148811	75			0	is	In the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list, click "Mail merge fields".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148841	76			0	is	In the\<emph\> Database selection\</emph\> box, double-click an address book, click "First Name", and then click\<emph\> Insert\</emph\>. Repeat for "Last Name".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147549	78			0	is	In the document, place the cursor between the two fields, press Space, and then return to the \<emph\>Fields \</emph\>dialog:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150416				0	is	Click the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab, and then click "Conditional text" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153589	146			0	is	In the \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box, type: "Addressbook.addresses.firstname".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153615	80			0	is	In the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>box, type a space and leave the \<emph\>Or \</emph\>box blank.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153562				0	is	You can now use a condition to insert text based on the contents of the First Name field.				20181231 09:50:43
